"jeong-sik","providerType":"User"},"email":"yousleepwhen@gmail.com","name":"jeong-sik"},"authoredDate":"2026-01-24T10:12:07Z","committedDate":"2026-01-24T10:12:07Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"jeong-sik","providerType":"User"},"email":"yousleepwhen@gmail.com","name":"jeong-sik"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:35:12.853Z","repositoryId":1140367480,"sha":"1b0ef81f622ee0621298b564bdd331765e713710"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:35:12.853Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/4be25af7cd5a22d6aeb187be326899e415ea94b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T02:14:05Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T02:14:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(etag): enforce RFC 7232 strong comparison on If-Match; SHA-256 digest (#111)\n\nTwo correctness/safety fixes in lib/etag.ml.\n\n1. If-Match must use strong comparison (RFC 7232 §3.1).\n\n   check_if_match reused parse_if_none_match + any_match, which\n   defaults to ~weak_comparison:true. A client could send\n\n     If-Match: W/\"v\"\n\n   against a server holding Strong \"v\" and pass the precondition.\n   That defeats the entire purpose of the header: two clients\n   holding weak validators of \"same\" semantic content could race\n   PUT/DELETE and the lost-update guard would silently let one of\n   them through, even though weak validators are explicitly not\n   sufficient for byte-equality reasoning.\n\n   Now: check_if_match runs strong-only comparison\n   (matches ~weak_comparison:false). Wildcard \"*\" still matches\n   anything per §3.1. If-None-Match still uses the default weak\n   comparison — that header''s semantics do allow it.\n\n2. SHA-256 instead of MD5 for the content fingerprint.\n\n   ETag''s job is \"different content => different tag\". MD5\n   collisions are practical, so an attacker who can influence\n   cached content can land two distinct bodies under the same\n   ETag and cause the cache to return stale or wrong content for\n   a subsequent request (cache poisoning class). SHA-256 closes\n   that without changing the public API: ETag values are opaque\n   to clients and 64 hex chars are within RFC limits. Existing\n   cached entries become one-shot misses on the upgrade.\n\nTests (6 new in test_etag_suite):\n\n  - if-match strong/strong passes (non-regression)\n  - if-match weak/strong rejected (the actual bug)\n  - if-match weak/weak rejected (strong-comparison contract)\n  - if-match wildcard passes (incl. weak server etag)\n  - if-match absent passes (no precondition)\n  - generate uses SHA-256 (length pin: 64 hex chars)\n\nThe SHA-256 length pin is a regression guard: a future \"perf\noptimization\" that flips back to MD5 (32 hex) trips this test\nspecifically rather than silently re-opening the collision class.\n\nFull suite passes.","tree":{"sha":"2d3201904d8e3646f948f3443b2258486038a972","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/2d3201904d8e3646f948f3443b2258486038a972"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/4be25af7cd5a22d6aeb187be326899e415ea94b7","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d3201904d8e3646f948f3443b2258486038a972\nparent 010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778724845 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778724845 +0900\n\nfix(etag): enforce RFC 7232 strong comparison on If-Match; SHA-256 digest (#111)\n\nTwo correctness/safety fixes in lib/etag.ml.\n\n1. If-Match must use strong comparison (RFC 7232 §3.1).\n\n   check_if_match reused parse_if_none_match + any_match, which\n   defaults to ~weak_comparison:true. A client could send\n\n     If-Match: W/\"v\"\n\n   against a server holding Strong \"v\" and pass the precondition.\n   That defeats the entire purpose of the header: two clients\n   holding weak validators of \"same\" semantic content could race\n   PUT/DELETE and the lost-update guard would silently let one of\n   them through, even though weak validators are explicitly not\n   sufficient for byte-equality reasoning.\n\n   Now: check_if_match runs strong-only comparison\n   (matches ~weak_comparison:false). Wildcard \"*\" still matches\n   anything per §3.1. If-None-Match still uses the default weak\n   comparison — that header''s semantics do allow it.\n\n2. SHA-256 instead of MD5 for the content fingerprint.\n\n   ETag''s job is \"different content => different tag\". MD5\n   collisions are practical, so an attacker who can influence\n   cached content can land two distinct bodies under the same\n   ETag and cause the cache to return stale or wrong content for\n   a subsequent request (cache poisoning class). SHA-256 closes\n   that without changing the public API: ETag values are opaque\n   to clients and 64 hex chars are within RFC limits. Existing\n   cached entries become one-shot misses on the upgrade.\n\nTests (6 new in test_etag_suite):\n\n  - if-match strong/strong passes (non-regression)\n  - if-match weak/strong rejected (the actual bug)\n  - if-match weak/weak rejected (strong-comparison contract)\n  - if-match wildcard passes (incl. weak server etag)\n  - if-match absent passes (no precondition)\n  - generate uses SHA-256 (length pin: 64 hex chars)\n\nThe SHA-256 length pin is a regression guard: a future \"perf\noptimization\" that flips back to MD5 (32 hex) trips this test\nspecifically rather than silently re-opening the collision class.\n\nFull suite passes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBS/tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzlAQABQzjkTUx2Dby9nPaQH3cDAH\nIdak2Ua2blEjnvGBd/VB+G5N9PpkZSoCoUkcenjkqAN44lCns3Nv9M9Lh1A5IpIw\nmdHrhvXbA68eqAj23Iv74NcpIj4VHdVRbUixbHuRAq7SspsgQAUh5GTXkExVa79/\nsS60bHks7vXL9MFtaKlPUkbeF2a9eE7jgf1EpuJvPZtT/EL/q0x1vVVlaO67h0PR\nnGPDrucFWS8dLUv+WrWlDSqa505IamasX0hFGrPKIpYIkUVYOgui5MSk/wPs7PT/\nMZUJFA2UGS5JIXHAKvoRFKr/xcw5gWH0CbGw1ExU2Rp4g1CRr4IWgiRcPiPI5wCv\nfw3rJB/tWQNQfOgAwZRxhTfwgNsaCsnojzygK/E0Kxp6KNE+auYikf12tRPvYqfz\n1z58MdlE22fdrDglCz2z+vSaDTcHZ3fm97aJH2HRZz3fGcQr7G+CxcI+7kJ37KkT\nzzBghh8lw7asUpGwLbSHysKDp1uAObp7VShQ1KXDJzLTqwhkPtCkxuFqbbnBGcLR\ncYUg6AWUVfbo4CsEIkG0oYAiGvDXBYsILx3WqISSZiULJ7U0PZ7cPIPgTKzsj86r\npPpunSizk9lSSdCtCeLGkpPS5tj83XXbPyab4TSZ5Neb5Asph4Ad5XK/z3NXFtOA\nvIPYtjn9vZGuQLYB/P2R\n=GdS1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-14T02:14:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/4be25af7cd5a22d6aeb187be326899e415ea94b7","node_id":"C_kwDOQ_igeNoAKDRiZTI1YWY3Y2Q1YTIyZDZhZWIxODdiZTMyNjg5OWU0MTVlYTk0Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb","sha":"010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb"}],"sha":"4be25af7cd5a22d6aeb187be326899e415ea94b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/4be25af7cd5a22d6aeb187be326899e415ea94b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T02:14:00Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T02:14:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cookie): reject CR/LF/NUL in Set-Cookie name and attribute values (#109)\n\nbuild_set_cookie interpolated name, path, domain, and expires straight\ninto the Set-Cookie header via sprintf. CR / LF / NUL are wire-level\nheader separators, so a caller that lands one of those bytes in any of\nthose fields would emit:\n\n  Set-Cookie: name=value\n  Set-Cookie: evil=1; Path=/\n\n— a Set-Cookie injection of a second arbitrary cookie. The shape that\nmakes this practically exploitable is dynamic name construction from\nuser input (e.g. \"pref-\" ^ user_id), which is a pattern that does\nappear in app code.\n\nUri.pct_encode is already applied to value, so CR/LF/NUL in value\nencode to percent-escape and cannot escape on the wire. Name is *not*\npct-encoded — that gate had no equivalent until this patch — and the\nthree attribute string fields are pure sprintf concat.\n\nThe fix adds reject_header_injection that walks the string and raises\nInvalid_argument on any byte in {0x0A, 0x0D, 0x00}. Other ASCII\ncontrols are not as universally header-fatal (tab is legal OWS), so\nthe reject set is intentionally narrow. The reject set is the minimum\nthat closes the injection — wider can be a separate posture decision.\n\nInvalid_argument is the right shape: callers of build_set_cookie are\nserver code, not end-user input parsers, so silently sanitizing would\nhide a programming bug. Loud failure surfaces the bug at test time.\n\nTests (5 new):\n\n  - build rejects CR/LF/NUL in name (three sub-cases)\n  - build rejects CRLF in path attribute\n  - build rejects CRLF in domain attribute\n  - build rejects CRLF in expires attribute\n  - value with CRLF is pct-encoded (defense-in-depth pin: future\n    refactors must not drop pct_encode from value alongside the\n    name/attribute validator — the existing wire-encoding behaviour\n    needs to keep working as the second line of defense)\n\nFull suite: all existing tests pass; new tests pin each rejection\npath individually so a \"simplification\" away from the validator\ntrips a specific case.","tree":{"sha":"3b5ee8d45b696c70a4bc794f5158bb9a093195d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/3b5ee8d45b696c70a4bc794f5158bb9a093195d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb","verification":{"payload":"tree 3b5ee8d45b696c70a4bc794f5158bb9a093195d2\nparent 4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778724840 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778724840 +0900\n\nfix(cookie): reject CR/LF/NUL in Set-Cookie name and attribute values (#109)\n\nbuild_set_cookie interpolated name, path, domain, and expires straight\ninto the Set-Cookie header via sprintf. CR / LF / NUL are wire-level\nheader separators, so a caller that lands one of those bytes in any of\nthose fields would emit:\n\n  Set-Cookie: name=value\n  Set-Cookie: evil=1; Path=/\n\n— a Set-Cookie injection of a second arbitrary cookie. The shape that\nmakes this practically exploitable is dynamic name construction from\nuser input (e.g. \"pref-\" ^ user_id), which is a pattern that does\nappear in app code.\n\nUri.pct_encode is already applied to value, so CR/LF/NUL in value\nencode to percent-escape and cannot escape on the wire. Name is *not*\npct-encoded — that gate had no equivalent until this patch — and the\nthree attribute string fields are pure sprintf concat.\n\nThe fix adds reject_header_injection that walks the string and raises\nInvalid_argument on any byte in {0x0A, 0x0D, 0x00}. Other ASCII\ncontrols are not as universally header-fatal (tab is legal OWS), so\nthe reject set is intentionally narrow. The reject set is the minimum\nthat closes the injection — wider can be a separate posture decision.\n\nInvalid_argument is the right shape: callers of build_set_cookie are\nserver code, not end-user input parsers, so silently sanitizing would\nhide a programming bug. Loud failure surfaces the bug at test time.\n\nTests (5 new):\n\n  - build rejects CR/LF/NUL in name (three sub-cases)\n  - build rejects CRLF in path attribute\n  - build rejects CRLF in domain attribute\n  - build rejects CRLF in expires attribute\n  - value with CRLF is pct-encoded (defense-in-depth pin: future\n    refactors must not drop pct_encode from value alongside the\n    name/attribute validator — the existing wire-encoding behaviour\n    needs to keep working as the second line of defense)\n\nFull suite: all existing tests pass; new tests pin each rejection\npath individually so a \"simplification\" away from the validator\ntrips a specific case.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBS/oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmugQAELyNeTdZAGmJ/pq6GLWalM2\nyPahs2Q9wOFn0zaz1e3ynYjtZuzmP/WihKm6m8FN+z299V3M3T1eKhrNDb8wSqJT\nz3J2NB1BNYuYhZbu3tD4c0pFpZDgIZe/Qw8LJCEY/HBCAKSLiUKmhye9PSMXuFR6\niN+7MAG6A8M4e22Jobq5Byn59iHkO5/5FJDzr4v0tX5pmGkBjtYDmaSDVJDhH5fy\nPf9J4vnWydFBQVIT0qkZ9PBTqXcBpVW8oEXNB3W+8XSRFUSO+ft4tc0jEAfCi4jp\nuRdJJV06SmjerbxCucc0y1g5vFhA22cMRTkrPnjWm4Y6fctO9XCxTSFJpmxjUG3p\n8KV+7iIY+Vk0ZpAI3RGEa7ZmTtdMG9ik0zSysCah2rNguOqqePhQ+L31ggZJWK/E\n8CSOl2VslMxyE/BoFgeAOBme+rDQ2SmGtEdKUg/n1k7LroOxDlEMxzR5TiVe+Sc/\nKl2cUA4pXaPotwkqfhc/EFWRW2VallXqMBXyINYrqI2z7Q6ecjHZwYEQTf5kjHZE\nMIWrXhhYU0YgO4sBGuUkTYdOS6EsuEitMvhIw3tByoOp7chgiA7SGqPQ3I/Ex1IN\nITwVUlskVj01e+4SIimEaveI/EeLQiV3HGXRzBMqLlC2TAeL6HMCXdP385ZXQDEe\n05iwfiGHBqzx8mTtIGcX\n=FN6j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-14T02:14:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb","node_id":"C_kwDOQ_igeNoAKDAxMGFmNTU2NWY3MzM0NmFmZmRhODZmNjNhY2QxNTJmNjQ1MDBhZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49","sha":"4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49"}],"sha":"010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/010af5565f73346affda86f63acd152f64500aeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T02:13:55Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T02:13:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(websocket): cap decoded frame payload at 16 MiB and reject 64-bit overflow (#108)\n\nThe frame decoder trusts the client-announced payload length unchanged.\nRFC 6455 permits a 64-bit length, but OCaml int on a 64-bit host is\nsigned 63-bit:\n\n  - A length of 2^31 forces the upstream reader to buffer 2 GiB before\n    decode_frame ever sees a complete frame. Nothing here emits the\n    1009 MessageTooBig close code RFC 6455 reserved for this case;\n    the framework simply waits.\n\n  - A 64-bit length with the high bit set wraps the lsl-or accumulator\n    into a negative OCaml int. The old code collapsed that into the\n    same \"Incomplete frame header\" string used for legitimate short\n    reads, so a caller built on the \"incomplete -> read more\" pattern\n    would keep buffering an attacker-chosen number of bytes.\n\nThis adds an explicit ?max_payload_size (default 16 MiB) and splits the\nlength-parse into three outcomes:\n\n  `Need_more  -> \"Incomplete frame header\"     (caller should buffer)\n  `Oversized  -> \"Payload length exceeds ...\"  (caller should close 1009)\n  `Ok (h, n)  -> proceed; further check vs max_payload_size\n\nThe high-bit-set 64-bit case is now `Oversized, never `Need_more.\nExisting callers compile unchanged (parameter is optional). The Kirin\nfacade ws_decode signature gains the same optional parameter.\n\nTests (3 new in test_websocket_suite):\n\n  1. decode rejects oversized payload (2 GiB announced, default cap).\n  2. decode respects custom cap (200 B announced, cap=100 rejects,\n     cap=1024 accepts) — non-regression for the default-cap behaviour.\n  3. decode rejects 64-bit high-bit-set length as oversized, with\n     the assertion checking the message class so a future refactor\n     cannot quietly route it back to \"incomplete\".\n\nFull suite green (1000+ tests).","tree":{"sha":"f26b2be3a103e72e28b2eda4be3dc1cd6dff5f2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/f26b2be3a103e72e28b2eda4be3dc1cd6dff5f2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49","verification":{"payload":"tree f26b2be3a103e72e28b2eda4be3dc1cd6dff5f2d\nparent 801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778724835 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778724835 +0900\n\nfix(websocket): cap decoded frame payload at 16 MiB and reject 64-bit overflow (#108)\n\nThe frame decoder trusts the client-announced payload length unchanged.\nRFC 6455 permits a 64-bit length, but OCaml int on a 64-bit host is\nsigned 63-bit:\n\n  - A length of 2^31 forces the upstream reader to buffer 2 GiB before\n    decode_frame ever sees a complete frame. Nothing here emits the\n    1009 MessageTooBig close code RFC 6455 reserved for this case;\n    the framework simply waits.\n\n  - A 64-bit length with the high bit set wraps the lsl-or accumulator\n    into a negative OCaml int. The old code collapsed that into the\n    same \"Incomplete frame header\" string used for legitimate short\n    reads, so a caller built on the \"incomplete -> read more\" pattern\n    would keep buffering an attacker-chosen number of bytes.\n\nThis adds an explicit ?max_payload_size (default 16 MiB) and splits the\nlength-parse into three outcomes:\n\n  `Need_more  -> \"Incomplete frame header\"     (caller should buffer)\n  `Oversized  -> \"Payload length exceeds ...\"  (caller should close 1009)\n  `Ok (h, n)  -> proceed; further check vs max_payload_size\n\nThe high-bit-set 64-bit case is now `Oversized, never `Need_more.\nExisting callers compile unchanged (parameter is optional). The Kirin\nfacade ws_decode signature gains the same optional parameter.\n\nTests (3 new in test_websocket_suite):\n\n  1. decode rejects oversized payload (2 GiB announced, default cap).\n  2. decode respects custom cap (200 B announced, cap=100 rejects,\n     cap=1024 accepts) — non-regression for the default-cap behaviour.\n  3. decode rejects 64-bit high-bit-set length as oversized, with\n     the assertion checking the message class so a future refactor\n     cannot quietly route it back to \"incomplete\".\n\nFull suite green (1000+ tests).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBS/kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkOwQAHryva6A+Af+CD2hHYeHdZEV\nf3orvVB/cJSIgkYa2/8G35SdYi/FyIhieGhtb+A+aOVrF68nuElJlIN+5YDqq/8N\nwINOZXv+Su47SgMAizIQd7uxVF4QiqIeBhDDBUzxo4De73c5wYN9YlcU80uzGzC6\ni2t4DJP4Pw8nMAvkwrHYJHO9fYIpxNTwL88Jcckmn/174rwBS4NwOt9WoJrgxhgo\nGMq4u5dy1KLj/178zhrRkli2VpvL4q9hEI+qVRYREU+rn8IrFQNBU+y8hnpcwJ9Q\naVhlC8TkZPSdRpy7hRn3l0Bx92C4ZSDyVawoGnyuU0HxsRKCyGAY36Nq0ng0x8M1\n8l4xJDEVD4svPTKYwwSvgtr0FiyS/fY/srQy8OU48gjkWX/f+6762NrhGXgnRiT8\nZU8KVA1q+2Pgh0MEyxk7EI/JDISaPq+OgVb07Hm9/y+0bESdA9eUBQ0daIu6F2WQ\ntXjWxKS7vEAZPtBP8tz86v3NGmcl/s/zZQYz1IafObLRtskQD/ajYl9To57ORJyn\nI6N0rieusax3qzKjVPEF8NK5iHKLCLlK33ZbX7GJ7MrhodIIsDmaSmBgw/45KIL3\nDY3uboQSqyRik8MxKO+pInuy9fVsPCggPM8EXwKjcEw1ly9yqNw7fYZPv6p5OOsG\nCCCywOZxSSS+yTa0//tW\n=71cX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-14T02:13:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49","node_id":"C_kwDOQ_igeNoAKDRhZjlmZmYyMTExOTgwOTFmNmFjYjQxOTBlYzM5YzBkNDFlYWJmNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c","sha":"801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c"}],"sha":"4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/4af9fff211198091f6acb4190ec39c0d41eabf49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-14T02:13:51Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-14T02:13:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(static): reject symlink escapes from the served directory (#107)\n\nThe textual contains_dot_dot check only blocks literal `..` segments in\nthe request path. It does not see filesystem-level symlinks, so a file\nunder dir whose inode is itself a symlink to /etc/passwd bypassed every\nguard: file_exists and is_directory both default to follow:true, and\nload_binary opens with default symlink semantics. A request for\n`/static/innocent.txt` would happily return the contents of the link\ntarget.\n\nAdd resolve_under which canonicalizes both dir and the candidate path\nwith Unix.realpath and requires the canonical candidate to sit under\nthe canonical dir (separator-bounded so dir vs dir-evil does not match).\nSymlinks that escape the served directory are now silently treated as\nnot-found (fall through to the next handler) rather than 403, so the\nresponse does not confirm the existence of the linked-to target.\n\nSymlinks that stay inside dir keep working — only the canonical form is\nrequired to be under dir, so versioned asset bundlers that emit\nwithin-dir symlinks are unaffected.\n\nTests (4 new):\n- regular file resolves\n- missing file falls through (not 403)\n- symlink within dir resolves (negative regression for over-restriction)\n- symlink to a file outside dir is rejected (the actual escape case)\n\nThe escape test creates a real symlink whose target is in a separate\ntemp dir and asserts resolve_under returns None. Negative-test the\nguard so it cannot decay into a dead branch in a future refactor.","tree":{"sha":"a86ce4eaad3c4ba9e3d21f32c288470c774126e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/a86ce4eaad3c4ba9e3d21f32c288470c774126e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c","verification":{"payload":"tree a86ce4eaad3c4ba9e3d21f32c288470c774126e5\nparent 219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778724831 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778724831 +0900\n\nfix(static): reject symlink escapes from the served directory (#107)\n\nThe textual contains_dot_dot check only blocks literal `..` segments in\nthe request path. It does not see filesystem-level symlinks, so a file\nunder dir whose inode is itself a symlink to /etc/passwd bypassed every\nguard: file_exists and is_directory both default to follow:true, and\nload_binary opens with default symlink semantics. A request for\n`/static/innocent.txt` would happily return the contents of the link\ntarget.\n\nAdd resolve_under which canonicalizes both dir and the candidate path\nwith Unix.realpath and requires the canonical candidate to sit under\nthe canonical dir (separator-bounded so dir vs dir-evil does not match).\nSymlinks that escape the served directory are now silently treated as\nnot-found (fall through to the next handler) rather than 403, so the\nresponse does not confirm the existence of the linked-to target.\n\nSymlinks that stay inside dir keep working — only the canonical form is\nrequired to be under dir, so versioned asset bundlers that emit\nwithin-dir symlinks are unaffected.\n\nTests (4 new):\n- regular file resolves\n- missing file falls through (not 403)\n- symlink within dir resolves (negative regression for over-restriction)\n- symlink to a file outside dir is rejected (the actual escape case)\n\nThe escape test creates a real symlink whose target is in a separate\ntemp dir and asserts resolve_under returns None. Negative-test the\nguard so it cannot decay into a dead branch in a future refactor.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBS/fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2IMQADb63g/UeCXxxjP9v+Fv69m5\nGFHhwARI0I73y0wP+ST9dYItAJ5T3+XwICA2a3h+2QfdKfxiRZvPlU+CWrh3qOI5\nXK8M9hwr4gTx13JvGvZdHzUOIlMsjwBiiP33eQR2XPa5YMuOW/85KdpSGEW1Q8GD\nY6i4N822CUPIbYwdLCbJlTMDUqfW4JUYzsTWiOPZnTidUe9XstLjYJuD+c3+K6pJ\nzjIP/wk9xKX7aJSTYYHDGKwsX3NqISEax1Ug2rxsK7r7ytJovZggs4WLMO/tSEKJ\nEZQnH27ksBfMzpOyPfQtzdHdj961nL+GX6TvuD+7n0afWcXB7N6xUfCvVFbEcgfn\nYxubmaNj+dFTNBkpjyrN01i9EJpzryZhh9TFt3xdSqJREym5KaUHrSlKTd5GtGx6\nHxZOzDCtl4exyLh5SCURARXoe80aNpefY5fwEsVmFGW3xrXoTJX5xB6zWurwMJQH\n4eIh0O8EJbM1SuA8Rnl4KeU4iceWo+rHWoyw52Jkl2xgdc8lJAY963IX36vAVZg6\ngmcCgekIc5fVpFh7UTOlfy9iQyzumPMosy0wuSmt1gyP2qin6hlSOPU27qEE+bUI\nPi4yjJhXQVBlHHX8E4vSe3aINJPOy16J3HiyL1/cItMRgfQFkghhmKnRWJzne3Jw\nC01prTGvXHKWLYKNgoPm\n=w1Jf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-14T02:13:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c","node_id":"C_kwDOQ_igeNoAKDgwMWZhMDczNTYxN2UxYTRjMmUxOTYzOTg0MWI1N2M1ZDI4NTg3MGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4","sha":"219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4"}],"sha":"801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/801fa0735617e1a4c2e19639841b57c5d285870c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T16:14:38Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T16:14:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(svelte,solid): thread route params from Request, drop placeholders (#85)\n\nIssue #77 medium finding: `svelte/handler.ml` and `solid/handler.ml`\nboth hard-coded `params = []` with a TODO. The router already stores\nmatched path segments in `Request.params`, and other adapters\n(react/astro/preact protocol) read `req.params` directly. The\nplaceholder silently dropped path params on every Svelte/Solid data\nload.\n\n- svelte/handler.ml:89 — load_handler reads req.Kirin.Request.params.\n- solid/handler.ml:88 — data_handler reads req.Kirin.Request.params.\n\n`solid/handler.mli` + `solid/kirin_solid.mli` had over-general\n`params:''b list` signatures that masked the missing wiring. Tightened\nto `params:Kirin.Request.params` ((string * string) list) so the\nloader callback type matches what callers actually receive.\n\nNo new exports. 99 svelte tests + solid suite green.","tree":{"sha":"24be3b5f6a79ec578bf8621b4333b8f03e08375e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/24be3b5f6a79ec578bf8621b4333b8f03e08375e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4","verification":{"payload":"tree 24be3b5f6a79ec578bf8621b4333b8f03e08375e\nparent bc72f666de21db1ffb0f8615db74907244092fb9\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778688878 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778688878 +0900\n\nfix(svelte,solid): thread route params from Request, drop placeholders (#85)\n\nIssue #77 medium finding: `svelte/handler.ml` and `solid/handler.ml`\nboth hard-coded `params = []` with a TODO. The router already stores\nmatched path segments in `Request.params`, and other adapters\n(react/astro/preact protocol) read `req.params` directly. The\nplaceholder silently dropped path params on every Svelte/Solid data\nload.\n\n- svelte/handler.ml:89 — load_handler reads req.Kirin.Request.params.\n- solid/handler.ml:88 — data_handler reads req.Kirin.Request.params.\n\n`solid/handler.mli` + `solid/kirin_solid.mli` had over-general\n`params:''b list` signatures that masked the missing wiring. Tightened\nto `params:Kirin.Request.params` ((string * string) list) so the\nloader callback type matches what callers actually receive.\n\nNo new exports. 99 svelte tests + solid suite green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBKNuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR1cQAE/je46tQVhAezjPe1d6SWhA\nZEzxElDG3jMyBMYQfmtae3Hjpe+fszpkqRAdwfLwgVs4Ie3yoVMJeBV5OSX6srhO\nllwO7A1elkrMppxuo5sPN/daRp+TsebXADFMsBP2bRFImp5Y/0wf7hwbqBlV3l6t\nfVt8u5hml9JrBFdrrQsbFHnL+z4a2Eiaul1tbdFq+UnkBzDD25omW2gaygXV0MbC\nxyz/e8CUH3xTr22r+MXbxdqXJrAVArAF8wf2j3x8Ex+Jj1YpRSQ2tx0uyc7SodOE\nQOoudIdozwmZzFgWlhYwg6I95RclR910q0Cs5U4oPjBvldWYx275b3+BunYWWihq\n2xGVhKh7vyHAIPPw/fyVe6NA3hpCFGdj9VpJmfXaBkL4X0QWx4vOj2eNieCkh03s\nnsMTMK5aqoB630ZNWZDxeO+BlZtEU20Jt3i+lQN7y0dCKMmAwyOUxkOiR1nbfTRy\nhdtiAbgTx2LHwUPHsrSdqdeICu6DdIXNbvTPcRlGpnQSw1CVWW7FVGnkE0VuwdZF\nhx71aMhnGfFe4XTYgomRBlbhOkCjAHhF/U8MMbeAYoPg6554Ao80TgNBDFrwciUN\nA/Cd3g2BSdfI7PWvpU5ThRIZ0KH9sBD7oGQxRJfQdWieZG8/VONH4RRgpPNycPWo\nDwnZAoV8+/u3c7eP/8NO\n=bxbt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T16:14:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4","node_id":"C_kwDOQ_igeNoAKDIxOWQxYmViY2Q4NGMzNzVkMWUwODhhMTcwMzIxNjE2MTY5MDY0YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/bc72f666de21db1ffb0f8615db74907244092fb9","sha":"bc72f666de21db1ffb0f8615db74907244092fb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/bc72f666de21db1ffb0f8615db74907244092fb9"}],"sha":"219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/219d1bebcd84c375d1e088a170321616169064a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/bc72f666de21db1ffb0f8615db74907244092fb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T16:14:35Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T16:14:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp/transport): add optional clock+timeout to HTTP send paths (#84)\n\nIssue #77 medium finding: send_http_request awaits a Promise without\na built-in deadline. Outside an enclosing Eio.Switch that may cancel,\nthis hangs the fiber forever.\n\nSurface change:\n\n  val send_http_request :\n    ?clock:[> float Eio.Time.clock_ty ] Eio.Resource.t ->\n    ?timeout:float ->\n    streamable_http_transport ->\n    Jsonrpc.request -> Jsonrpc.response\n\nWhen both [clock] and [timeout] are passed, the await is wrapped in\n[Eio.Time.with_timeout]. On expiry the pending entry is deregistered\n(so a late server response cannot resolve a stale resolver) and\n[Transport_error] is raised. Omitting either keeps the historical\nunbounded await for back-compat — all existing call sites continue to\ntype-check unchanged.\n\n[send_request] mirrors the optional parameters and forwards them to\nthe HTTP path. Stdio ignores them (line-based read, no Eio scheduling\nprimitive available).\n\nTest: send_http_request with timeout=0.05s, no resolver, asserts\nTransport_error is raised and the pending list size returns to the\npre-call value (deregistration verified).","tree":{"sha":"84f7b75510c52fb370690cfcfda20375d76241ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/84f7b75510c52fb370690cfcfda20375d76241ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/bc72f666de21db1ffb0f8615db74907244092fb9","verification":{"payload":"tree 84f7b75510c52fb370690cfcfda20375d76241ce\nparent 1cdd7d10c764fb04d7c40d36f66ef843aaf8348c\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778688875 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778688875 +0900\n\nfeat(mcp/transport): add optional clock+timeout to HTTP send paths (#84)\n\nIssue #77 medium finding: send_http_request awaits a Promise without\na built-in deadline. Outside an enclosing Eio.Switch that may cancel,\nthis hangs the fiber forever.\n\nSurface change:\n\n  val send_http_request :\n    ?clock:[> float Eio.Time.clock_ty ] Eio.Resource.t ->\n    ?timeout:float ->\n    streamable_http_transport ->\n    Jsonrpc.request -> Jsonrpc.response\n\nWhen both [clock] and [timeout] are passed, the await is wrapped in\n[Eio.Time.with_timeout]. On expiry the pending entry is deregistered\n(so a late server response cannot resolve a stale resolver) and\n[Transport_error] is raised. Omitting either keeps the historical\nunbounded await for back-compat — all existing call sites continue to\ntype-check unchanged.\n\n[send_request] mirrors the optional parameters and forwards them to\nthe HTTP path. Stdio ignores them (line-based read, no Eio scheduling\nprimitive available).\n\nTest: send_http_request with timeout=0.05s, no resolver, asserts\nTransport_error is raised and the pending list size returns to the\npre-call value (deregistration verified).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBKNrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHP8QAIIRPmhwWeoFKg0OjCBNJuc5\n/0w1d2JqJQZlbhH8Pl2UthnhFRA2OVuIDZ4yjjMbktz2y0XXaIFc6EJw/tevvFRv\nZTdK4p86ZKabO81pFhnWIna5HzV2/6nPudD67RnpiyGHDHVuWrAlHWVL6wkjrLp+\n5OT6X+oPeEbpCdD1E/vTA7A2vj11kjYjuqSyyWwL/LZ+vxkz3TR8TUp0zWNJIT37\n0gsNN8W3oCnjjn8Jje5otJpptErrbGdDYkiL6waHL3k1FcqTaZBB4Ha/5e9LUQ0k\nN3fWfQxzDECpbnW8xKR4NLW98TqTFxXTMKd/Brto04Y03WRR66ykSzBsttJB02xg\n1b+RBUqgRFBJNiAEPfT6/qi1O+RU2gV5QumznKmMopfX9HojgR5GQWl/HHqARQhX\nYADxZa/eNLFsupzsV0T2CMF1OzBzCsclvCBAW0SU3vm5OGeOWqB36YMHXUn2dZee\nEg1z+MLzXjjnMnGqFRPDOyH/DBp2n2qrtMWdn6fO6NyW1XOI/+PDS4PfMOPN5Hu1\nSP5V7pp2X917frAEGuVLxWDxdLSJajQJBzHuaxoBNQuMLLobM8Q2129tAm07nPG5\nQgg8JoxcDKTLKCp5SXTcyJtwha5L1KjS0/YNlZtEtE79SEIbJfOD25IvaggD0rTS\nK2diMfthMdjQnW2yKXYr\n=rqxY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T16:14:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://a