_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/1cdd7d10c764fb04d7c40d36f66ef843aaf8348c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T16:14:31Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T16:14:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: replace Unix.sleepf with Eio.Time.sleep in test code (#83)\n\n`Unix.sleepf` blocks the OS thread — incorrect in Eio test contexts\nwhere the runtime expects fiber-yielding sleeps. Per issue #75, swap\nto `Eio.Time.sleep (Eio.Stdenv.clock env) 0.01` at 6 call sites:\n\n- test_cache.ml (4): tests already had `Eio_main.run` — captured env\n  and used the env''s clock. Dropped now-unused `unix` lib dep.\n- test_health_suite.ml (1): wrapped test body in `Eio_main.run` to\n  obtain a clock; already runs under `test_kirin` group with eio_main.\n- test_trace.ml (1): added `eio` + `eio_main` deps (was `unix`), wrapped\n  body in `Eio_main.run`.\n\nNo production code touched. Closes #75 (test code path).\n\nThe 3 pre-existing flakes (Cache ttl, Cache cleanup, Metrics\nhistogram time) are unrelated — fixed by PR #82.","tree":{"sha":"747975c0c8a6c8925a1de2c64fa6472a1abf6180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/747975c0c8a6c8925a1de2c64fa6472a1abf6180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/1cdd7d10c764fb04d7c40d36f66ef843aaf8348c","verification":{"payload":"tree 747975c0c8a6c8925a1de2c64fa6472a1abf6180\nparent d0ad798ec07339f179472ada6b71eec32df28858\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778688871 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778688871 +0900\n\ntest: replace Unix.sleepf with Eio.Time.sleep in test code (#83)\n\n`Unix.sleepf` blocks the OS thread — incorrect in Eio test contexts\nwhere the runtime expects fiber-yielding sleeps. Per issue #75, swap\nto `Eio.Time.sleep (Eio.Stdenv.clock env) 0.01` at 6 call sites:\n\n- test_cache.ml (4): tests already had `Eio_main.run` — captured env\n  and used the env''s clock. Dropped now-unused `unix` lib dep.\n- test_health_suite.ml (1): wrapped test body in `Eio_main.run` to\n  obtain a clock; already runs under `test_kirin` group with eio_main.\n- test_trace.ml (1): added `eio` + `eio_main` deps (was `unix`), wrapped\n  body in `Eio_main.run`.\n\nNo production code touched. Closes #75 (test code path).\n\nThe 3 pre-existing flakes (Cache ttl, Cache cleanup, Metrics\nhistogram time) are unrelated — fixed by PR #82.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBKNnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAME0QAKjkM6VSgimDs4+q6eqMZajO\n+/0KaanrAmmPgDfUdwz/eL7Gtr+BERUsND0fkRmFQOEGWKWOj8A4sBwkAXsHJy0l\nZL2qkUGmi0vks/0KRD6T+Jd+9yoVCf/V1nPF9iYMd0O1uvqN79D/ZtxObgmLDSo5\nzTUvR0r/54UcjDk+rjrmtYrnrJ+E1KaFdMZWjP7m/SUF55tzkfWvRDuT4yQyprQw\n7Fg6TefxDs9re7TXM//GrPKvZYEruU0NKxDJrN6+QYF7x4iEnnCSAx7m/lzYv1RA\nc6piA9Y6YwfvttchfArLEeuUJSSee/bjng/SB/ulKs4vOfsaVDaOO4bpv1AsbYhe\nJEL63014EYhBcwfKEcVjsmnc23PLTFfVIf6dTZ+987H+HNfrOO4DDrZ8rCmobCad\nmGzEhaTDuocrYN+kVYjMlX5bt4ySF59IgJ2ZPKvJFG6skz13Ynhj1otW/6bwVcF4\nj8h1lB5Fyn244Qgo06lLYUwPtpktohzqAcjX5IIuE8fTe/YquCAHkFPRcJOZ2bPQ\nhJjG+LrKfXkYDgzH6s1JEypL0QtZyHBY8nP5ZuxRvx/CHRZ5VGqZ4SLDRj6jML5N\nmrN7cenEwUnwRgPymW4+Xm8O78TcYtUm1QaYaIk4MGBQZ01RR+8aBuQsHGkLxGhr\nSUn3L/UQzeF8twUEH4bC\n=4Sjh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-13T16:14:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/1cdd7d10c764fb04d7c40d36f66ef843aaf8348c","node_id":"C_kwDOQ_igeNoAKDFjZGQ3ZDEwYzc2NGZiMDRkN2M0MGQzNmY2NmVmODQzYWFmODM0OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/d0ad798ec07339f179472ada6b71eec32df28858","sha":"d0ad798ec07339f179472ada6b71eec32df28858","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/d0ad798ec07339f179472ada6b71eec32df28858"}],"sha":"1cdd7d10c764fb04d7c40d36f66ef843aaf8348c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/1cdd7d10c764fb04d7c40d36f66ef843aaf8348c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/d0ad798ec07339f179472ada6b71eec32df28858/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T16:14:06Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T16:14:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: initialize Time_compat clock inside with_eio helper (#82)\n\nThree suites (Cache ttl, Cache cleanup, Metrics histogram time) call\n`Kirin.Time_compat.sleep` which dereferences a global Eio clock set via\n`Time_compat.set_clock`. That setter is only invoked inside `Kirin.run` —\nthe test runner enters `Alcotest.run` directly, so for any test that uses\nthe time API the clock stays uninitialized and the assertion path raises:\n\n  Time_compat: clock not initialized. Call Time_compat.set_clock during\n  Eio.main before using sleep.\n\nThe split in #72 surfaced this regression because the previous monolithic\ntest_kirin.ml used a single Eio_main.run wrapper that happened to keep\nthose tests inside `Kirin.run`''s reach.\n\nFix: have `with_eio` (already the shared Eio entry helper for these\nsuites) call `Kirin.Time_compat.set_clock` on the current\n`Eio.Stdenv.clock` before yielding to the test body. The setter is a plain\nref assignment, so re-running per test is harmless. All 210 cases now\npass locally (3 prior failures clear).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"efd004ef07599b1d929ddb83abce07f950cba961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/efd004ef07599b1d929ddb83abce07f950cba961"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/d0ad798ec07339f179472ada6b71eec32df28858","verification":{"payload":"tree efd004ef07599b1d929ddb83abce07f950cba961\nparent 340bef35469aa081721282e4f9a180bdefb62554\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778688846 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778688846 +0900\n\ntest: initialize Time_compat clock inside with_eio helper (#82)\n\nThree suites (Cache ttl, Cache cleanup, Metrics histogram time) call\n`Kirin.Time_compat.sleep` which dereferences a global Eio clock set via\n`Time_compat.set_clock`. That setter is only invoked inside `Kirin.run` —\nthe test runner enters `Alcotest.run` directly, so for any test that uses\nthe time API the clock stays uninitialized and the assertion path raises:\n\n  Time_compat: clock not initialized. Call Time_compat.set_clock during\n  Eio.main before using sleep.\n\nThe split in #72 surfaced this regression because the previous monolithic\ntest_kirin.ml used a single Eio_main.run wrapper that happened to keep\nthose tests inside `Kirin.run`''s reach.\n\nFix: have `with_eio` (already the shared Eio entry helper for these\nsuites) call `Kirin.Time_compat.set_clock` on the current\n`Eio.Stdenv.clock` before yielding to the test body. The setter is a plain\nref assignment, so re-running per test is harmless. All 210 cases now\npass locally (3 prior failures clear).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqBKNPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxRoQAFgrvKkk0uah4JzSrYQK0rAc\n9XBzlVvA+LlSgxtJExuEyJediI5MEKa5Q8Ouf1cpYz97Mk0Y0uFhFhtWNSo89iJE\n1qlpBErueHd1Pj+B7cfKcqaXcpT3ekMx7vIAcOp1dNXftLkQ49X28ZRFpY9Nmw6c\nkCWKGzB8lxIa43Pwv6TIHRA6A8rGF9Ac3zC4liEinpaFljOGxJKZ6UqwKfxRRit8\n57MQ44jRvM0WhYR/46CpsLDwaQways02Kd4LV9mgbe/lc/KixANDN229mbFtwS7d\nsoL05rDgQiM5XrymOesIgCdxcovxvMMkYsp/Lk34LGW/LGItidezKzoIutfQSmmi\notvUV41nIvvxf1AsDE6euMZDI0+m8ePvnBluUcmh4/bjNz/9PVvyqrPEaDWlhlRt\nd0TKnRftFML9KkC7MRYWA