github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/340bef35469aa081721282e4f9a180bdefb62554/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T14:16:15Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T14:16:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): track mcp-protocol-sdk merge — depend on unified mcp_protocol package (#81)\n\n* fix(deps): track mcp-protocol-sdk merge — depend on unified mcp_protocol package\n\nmcp-protocol-sdk merged its three opam packages (mcp_protocol, mcp_protocol_eio,\nmcp_protocol_http) into a single mcp_protocol opam package in PR #60\n(2026-03-27), keeping the OCaml-level library `mcp_protocol_eio` as\n`(public_name mcp_protocol.eio)` inside it. Downstream consumers that still\ndeclare `mcp_protocol_eio` as an opam dep break with:\n\n  [NOTE] Package mcp_protocol_eio does not exist in opam repositories...\n  [ERROR] No valid package definition found for mcp_protocol_eio\n\nThis has been silently breaking GitHub-triggered Railway builds for wkbl since\n2026-03-27 (every PR build failing at `opam install`).\n\nChanges:\n- dune-project: depend on `mcp_protocol >= 1.0.0` instead of\n  `mcp_protocol_eio >= 0.15.0`.\n- lib/dune: reference `mcp_protocol.eio` (public_name) rather than the bare\n  internal library name. Source code (`lib/time_compat.ml` uses\n  `Mcp_protocol_eio.Time_compat`) is unchanged — the OCaml-level library name\n  is preserved upstream.\n- kirin.opam: regenerated by `dune build`. Also brings the file in sync with\n  dune-project''s `(version 2.1.4)` that was already on main.\n\nVerified: `dune build` clean. Test suite has 3 timing-sensitive flakes (Cache\nttl, Cache cleanup, Metrics histogram time) that reproduce on origin/main too\nand are unrelated to this change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: drop obsolete mcp_protocol_eio / mcp_protocol_http opam pins\n\nThese were transitive deps of the old, pre-merge mcp-protocol-sdk layout. The\nupstream repo merged its three opam packages into a single `mcp_protocol`\npackage on 2026-03-27 (mcp-protocol-sdk#60). Pinning the old names now fails\nwith `No valid package definition found for mcp_protocol_eio`, which is why\nthe build matrix on this PR went red.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"72c40524fecd8a8c4ca5431c567d1edf41693709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/72c40524fecd8a8c4ca5431c567d1edf41693709"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/340bef35469aa081721282e4f9a180bdefb62554","verification":{"payload":"tree 72c40524fecd8a8c4ca5431c567d1edf41693709\nparent 4a1f1b4a71784078b41e96e95d8574b1ead1ca93\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1778681775 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778681775 +0900\n\nfix(deps): track mcp-protocol-sdk merge — depend on unified mcp_protocol package (#81)\n\n* fix(deps): track mcp-protocol-sdk merge — depend on unified mcp_protocol package\n\nmcp-protocol-sdk merged its three opam packages (mcp_protocol, mcp_protocol_eio,\nmcp_protocol_http) into a single mcp_protocol opam package in PR #60\n(2026-03-27), keeping the OCaml-level library `mcp_protocol_eio` as\n`(public_name mcp_protocol.eio)` inside it. Downstream consumers that still\ndeclare `mcp_protocol_eio` as an opam dep break with:\n\n  [NOTE] Package mcp_protocol_eio does not exist in opam repositories...\n  [ERROR] No valid package definition found for mcp_protocol_eio\n\nThis has been silently breaking GitHub-triggered Railway builds for wkbl since\n2026-03-27 (every PR build failing at `opam install`).\n\nChanges:\n- dune-project: depend on `mcp_protocol >= 1.0.0` instead of\n  `mcp_protocol_eio >= 0.15.0`.\n- lib/dune: reference `mcp_protocol.eio` (public_name) rather than the bare\n  internal library name. Source code (`lib/time_compat.ml` uses\n  `Mcp_protocol_eio.Time_compat`) is unchanged — the OCaml-level library name\n  is preserved upstream.\n- kirin.opam: regenerated by `dune build`. Also brings the file in sync with\n  dune-project''s `(version 2.1.4)` that was already on main.\n\nVerified: `dune build` clean. Test suite has 3 timing-sensitive flakes (Cache\nttl, Cache cleanup, Metrics histogram time) that reproduce on origin/main too\nand are unrelated to this change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: drop obsolete mcp_protocol_eio / mcp_protocol_http opam pins\n\nThese were transitive deps of the old, pre-merge mcp-protocol-sdk layout. The\nupstream repo merged its three opam packages into a single `mcp_protocol`\npackage on 2026-03-27 (mcp-protocol-sdk#60). Pinning the old names now fails\nwith `No valid package definition found for mcp_protocol_eio`, which is why\nthe build matrix on this PR went red.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-