_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/ad3f8cd4194a9a4dcbc8edde80e0320dd7de2118","sha":"ad3f8cd4194a9a4dcbc8edde80e0320dd7de2118","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/ad3f8cd4194a9a4dcbc8edde80e0320dd7de2118"}],"sha":"7e6a3f68f187f587c853f3a8bef7bbddb0b8576c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/7e6a3f68f187f587c853f3a8bef7bbddb0b8576c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/ad3f8cd4194a9a4dcbc8edde80e0320dd7de2118/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-17T02:47:20Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-17T02:47:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf+fix: cache O(1) LRU, metric optimizations, .mli abstractions (#25)\n\n* perf(cache): replace O(n) list with O(1) hashtbl for LRU tracking\n\nThe access_order list caused O(n) filter on every get/set (touch_key).\nReplace with a (key, float) Hashtbl for access timestamps:\n- touch is now O(1) (Hashtbl.replace)\n- eviction scans for min timestamp O(n) but only when cache is full\n- Also make (''k, ''v) t and ''a entry abstract in cache.mli (H8)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(metrics): replace list with circular array in metric_summary\n\n- observe was O(n) due to List.length on every call\n- quantile was O(n log n + n) due to List.sort + List.nth\n- Now uses a fixed-size circular buffer array:\n  - observe is O(1) (array write + index bump)\n  - quantile caches sorted array, invalidated on mutation\n  - length tracked explicitly to avoid recomputation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(metrics): extract Metric_common module for shared label type and with_lock\n\n- New metric_common.ml/.mli with shared label type and with_lock helper\n- metric_counter, metric_gauge, metric_histogram, metric_summary,\n  metric_prometheus now use Metric_common.label and Metric_common.with_lock\n- Removes duplicated with_lock definitions (was in 5 files)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(metrics): add accessor functions, abstract .mli types, normalize path labels\n\n- Add name/help/label_names/iter_values accessors to counter, gauge, histogram, summary\n- Replace direct field access in metric_prometheus.ml with accessor calls\n- Add sum/count accessors to metric_summary for Prometheus export\n- Add default_normalize_path to middleware preventing label cardinality explosion\n- Update metrics.mli signature with ?normalize_path parameter\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(cache): use monotonic counter instead of float timestamp for LRU ordering\n\nFloat timestamps had insufficient precision for rapid sequential operations,\ncausing non-deterministic eviction when multiple keys were added within the\nsame gettimeofday resolution window.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: bump version to 1.0.1\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a9aef174dfa7841e1f0ed5235f17f0d4251b8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/0a9aef174dfa7841e1f0ed5235f17f0d4251b8fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/ad3f8cd4194a9a4dcbc8edde80e0320dd7de2118","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a9aef174dfa7841e1f0ed5235f17f0d4251b8fc\nparent 4df70aa5da21cc78d5bb12fa76262794474e6ece\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1773715640 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773715640 +0900\n\nperf+fix: cache O(1) LRU, metric optimizations, .mli abstractions (#25)\n\n* perf(cache): replace O(n) list with O(1) hashtbl for LRU tracking\n\nThe access_order list caused O(n) filter on every get/set (touch_key).\nReplace with a (key, float) Hashtbl for access timestamps:\n- touch is now O(1) (Hashtbl.replace)\n- eviction scans for min timestamp O(n) but only when cache is full\n- Also make (''k, ''v) t and ''a entry abstract in cache.mli (H8)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(metrics): replace list with circular array in metric_summary\n\n- observe was O(n) due to List.length on every call\n- quantile was O(n log n + n) due to List.sort + List.nth\n- Now uses a fixed-size circular buffer array:\n  - observe is O(1) (array write + index bump)\n  - quantile caches sorted array, invalidated on mutation\n  - length tracked explicitly to avoid recomputation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(metrics): extract Metric_common module for shared label type and with_lock\n\n- New metric_common.ml/.mli with shared label type and with_lock helper\n- metric_counter, metric_gauge, metric_histogram, metric_summary,\n  metric_prometheus now use Metric_common.label and Metric_common.with_lock\n- Removes duplicated with_lock definitions (was in 5 files)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(metrics): add accessor functions, abstract .mli types, normalize path labels\n\n- Add name/help/label_names/iter_values accessors to counter, gauge, histogram, summary\n- Replace direct field access in metric_prometheus.ml with accessor calls\n- Add sum/count accessors to metric_summary for Prometheus export\n- Add default_normalize_path to middleware preventing label cardinality explosion\n- Update metrics.mli signature with ?normalize_path parameter\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(cache): use monotonic counter instead of float timestamp for LRU ordering\n\nFloat timestamps had insufficient precision for rapid sequential operations,\ncausing non-deterministic eviction when multiple keys were added within the\nsame gettimeofday resolution window.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: bump version to 1.0.1\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpuMC4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT7sQAFGiLnNyu0E7/Wltbbw+KGNc\n5enFey518+2S4CoCVCUNwlmDuilnhXB76IHlVdEBGG6NLl+3MT7yMihddA9XFovC\nz9B0jhQaXSr6L0QriBXc3wRxg7Ih/uCcnNgryPPG+OhRmBhy0pwSteytT8gRmlrd\ndMR8I2cHNx4kWIBBABHzBH6bg+oi7j738YEY8ioCmX1TSfLMhl1gl9/HOurJI/NC\n3zbjQv3a1mCJLDw0CDKFGbqcMG3P+LQmiD2FK3twSSvXdWghpYuWu4fgL2rF3hlH\njnJkyaKZon/1V+seG5+Qr+BATKVD//B1+Hq1mxo367EbUSBI3MrBhQuduLLTzcrX\n/2TAMwSUno4VuGQTvjWA0lUVM/7mLtOHh7baaY5vyfSlbzsiWwHBdh78syvqY9JV\nOx+hVy7EYu2VkJn1cRRYQmtl1IrSPiQqUQzN0cwTrN5IfE7u3jroyAYNdSoZSmKM\nh85TIvZdzSPB43dmOn02nMAgR0TVvxGyEJXzyzBLVYQYYwSniXxKdGOpTNIw6ImH\nwygt6apmVbnX1a5rWHDN9XxcaBUa8r0XMN0f0UaQJ45omg2nKUXX7knGqlNkBO4i\nU/sbuRBkQO3BLZjn18bB64ATycr/jCt1Fylljs9C8eBjoU/OACuhhVS8NLF3h34y\n0ZR49zq4oo1EI6f+MfBQ\n=CY1P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verifi