a76262794474e6ece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/4df70aa5da21cc78d5bb12fa76262794474e6ece"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/07f719649f88ea7e44dcd75b8f74b20e82d019ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-08T17:06:38Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-08T17:06:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(webrtc)!: replace mock with real ocaml-webrtc wrapper (v1.0.0) (#22)\n\n* feat(webrtc): add .mli interfaces for WebRTC modules\n\nDefine stable API surface for webrtc_config, webrtc_adapter, and\nwebrtc_signaling. Preparation for v1.0.0 real WebRTC integration.\n\n- webrtc_config.mli: ice_state, ice_candidate, session_description,\n  sdp_type, datachannel_state/options, stun_server/ice_servers types\n- webrtc_adapter.mli: DataChannel and PeerConnection modules with\n  full record types exposed (to be made opaque in Phase 2),\n  Signaling re-export, HTTP/WebSocket handler signatures\n- webrtc_signaling.mli: message variant type, encode/decode,\n  room/server management API\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(webrtc)!: replace mock with real ocaml-webrtc wrapper (v1.0.0)\n\nReplace 303-line mock PeerConnection/DataChannel with thin wrapper\naround ocaml-webrtc. webrtc_config.ml re-exports Ice.connection_state\nfor type equality. webrtc_adapter.ml follows grpc.ml re-export pattern.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Kirin.WebRTC.PeerConnection and Kirin.WebRTC.DataChannel\nmodules removed. Use Kirin.WebRTC.create_peer, create_datachannel, and\nKirin.WebRTC.Peer module instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address GLM-5 review — connection_state type, dead API removal, ICE role mapping\n\n- Rename ice_state (7 ICE variants) to connection_state (6 Webrtc_eio variants)\n  for correct type equality with Peer.get_state\n- Remove dead types: datachannel_state, datachannel_options, default_datachannel_options\n- Add ICE role mapping: Client→Controlling, Server→Controlled in create_peer\n- Add placeholder DTLS fingerprint warnings to create_offer/create_answer docs\n- Fix test assertions to match actual JSON encoder output (offer, ice-candidate)\n- Update CHANGELOG with breaking type rename and dead API removal\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3e954c58b6a5cc84d71266f4055455ffe7a6a1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/d3e954c58b6a5cc84d71266f4055455ffe7a6a1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/07f719649f88ea7e44dcd75b8f74b20e82d019ae","verification":{"payload":"tree d3e954c58b6a5cc84d71266f4055455ffe7a6a1a\nparent 819746cfb807d04bfd7eb9e00edf941358555133\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1772989598 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772989598 +0900\n\nfeat(webrtc)!: replace mock with real ocaml-webrtc wrapper (v1.0.0) (#22)\n\n* feat(webrtc): add .mli interfaces for WebRTC modules\n\nDefine stable API surface for webrtc_config, webrtc_adapter, and\nwebrtc_signaling. Preparation for v1.0.0 real WebRTC integration.\n\n- webrtc_config.mli: ice_state, ice_candidate, session_description,\n  sdp_type, datachannel_state/options, stun_server/ice_servers types\n- webrtc_adapter.mli: DataChannel and PeerConnection modules with\n  full record types exposed (to be made opaque in Phase 2),\n  Signaling re-export, HTTP/WebSocket handler signatures\n- webrtc_signaling.mli: message variant type, encode/decode,\n  room/server management API\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(webrtc)!: replace mock with real ocaml-webrtc wrapper (v1.0.0)\n\nReplace 303-line mock PeerConnection/DataChannel with thin wrapper\naround ocaml-webrtc. webrtc_config.ml re-exports Ice.connection_state\nfor type equality. webrtc_adapter.ml follows grpc.ml re-export pattern.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Kirin.WebRTC.PeerConnection and Kirin.WebRTC.DataChannel\nmodules removed. Use Kirin.WebRTC.create_peer, create_datachannel, and\nKirin.WebRTC.Peer module instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address GLM-5 review — connection_state type, dead API removal, ICE role mapping\n\n- Rename ice_state (7 ICE variants) to connection_state (6 Webrtc_eio variants)\n  for correct type equality with Peer.get_state\n- Remove dead types: datachannel_state, datachannel_options, default_datachannel_options\n- Add ICE role mapping: Client→Controlling, Server→Controlled in create_peer\n- Add placeholder DTLS fingerprint warnings to create_offer/create_answer docs\n- Fix test assertions to match actual JSON encoder output (offer, ice-candidate)\n- Update CHANGELOG with breaking type rename and dead API removal\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJprayeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFScQAKRY83dZFGFuzc/fGg225sme\nRRpn+DtQ7ljRQE1Q5x1XucaosPojRNFl3Ahb/2MYVH9WBO3KMtfghQQvptKK+hLx\nPZiYu4AiL4/coTIgdSjejIqR3Hd8Oe8IkoCsBWKFq1aRay+IMchv6QacRnzsdyGx\nE18eIMgjA8llGUARO8HUCf1T/BY7dUAzd/3i9uUP1yuJWndCHqJs8AF77lCAeDN2\n3cKYbM62Rcff3PXdWFsm5PE/x7b4v+FpPPL8cqAMUiujzl3s0rqaoI1qHr/1zARC\n6mkmMxyfy2vjj9lIQI5M2xvVXem8X98ZLfbHSp/SobNkuNlff7Afmb9PLp0GALp+\n8IG8AnGzLDDMg2PfGfAcOctRBPfHepmj09Pip7GP+8K7VEyoouUHitIGjrYDvLYZ\n9x1C559LXjI2KsLJsG3lL3Qwq1+FrkmKyD1XX4CzRnMBYjifamyOoNxsYr30DWUg\nT4B+A0mymA7SJAio5wAOd5bK7AVZ0fW+Lwu+yrM8S9Y7qF+koorhxAPGylXAC030\nJUnXuKXatsHHefEb/VZW4q4hUJIoEPzTHvBeuzk163b8jaVsEnZGalLZs4kEvO6Q\nYPzsTokRlyuGm8/glxFks0NWimvaW/xxnx88JYdhXk8r5v8LjujM3KQ/POBKM0aj\n58E3fdCdd+vVxams5tkP\n=LZyi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-08T17:06:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/07f719649f88ea7e44dcd75b8f74b20e82d019ae","node_id":"C_kwDOQ_igeNoAKDA3ZjcxOTY0OWY4OGVhN2U0NGRjZDc1YjhmNzRiMjBlODJkMDE5YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/819746cfb807d04bfd7eb9e00edf941358555133","sha":"819746cfb807d04bfd7eb9e00edf941358555133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/819746cfb807d04bfd7eb9e00edf941358555133"}],"sha":"07f719649f88ea7e44dcd75b8f74b20e82d019ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/07f719649f88ea7e44dcd75b8f74b20e82d019ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/819746cfb807d04bfd7eb9e00edf941358555133/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-07T17:33:27Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-07T17:33:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(kirin)!: v0.9.0 — Stream EOS safety, file splits, .mli expansion (#21)\n\n* feat(kirin)!: v0.9.0 — Stream EOS type safety, file splits, .mli expansion\n\nBreaking: `Response.body` Stream/Producer variants now use\n`string option Eio.Stream.t` — `None` signals end-of-stream instead of\nempty string sentinel. Prevents false EOS on protocols where empty\nstring is valid data. Public `yielder`/`producer` types unchanged.\n\nBatch 1 (GLM review carryover):\n- Stream EOS: `string` → `string option` across response, server,\n  stream, sse (7 files). New tests: None-terminates, empty-string-\n  passes-through.\n- Traceparent: `parse_traceparent` now validates lowercase hex chars\n  per W3C Trace Context spec. Tests: uppercase reject, non-hex reject.\n- Random seeding: `Random.self_init ()` at module init for trace ID\n  uniqueness.\n\nBatch 2 (file splits via `include` pattern, public API unchanged):\n- validation.ml 620→430 lines (+validation_schema.ml, +validation_format.ml)\n- testing.ml 563→60 facade (+5 sub-modules)\n- webrtc_adapter.ml 512→302 (+webrtc_config.ml, +webrtc_signaling.ml)\n- metrics.ml 421→154 facade (+5 sub-modules)\n\nBatch 3 (.mli expansion + CI):\n- 8 new .mli files: trace, backpressure, cache, validation, metrics,\n  websocket, sse, cookie. Total: 15 interface files.\n- CI coverage gate: 50% → 60%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(stream): guarantee EOS delivery via Fun.protect\n\nGLM-5 review finding: if producer raises an exception, None (EOS)\nwas never sent to the stream, causing consumer fiber to hang\nindefinitely. Wrap all 3 producer functions (response, file_response,\nfile_inline) with Fun.protect ~finally to guarantee EOS delivery.\n\nAlso narrow broad exception in webrtc_signaling.ml decode_message\nfrom catch-all to Yojson.Safe.Util.Type_error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update CHANGELOG with GLM-5 review fixes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3653e4844d0373c7c55a67b7ea249691538edf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/c3653e4844d0373c7c55a67b7ea249691538edf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/819746cfb807d04bfd7eb9e00edf941358555133","verification":{"payload":"tree c3653e4844d0373c7c55a67b7ea249691538edf3\nparent bf87766f1ca5d2cfdef68a8cd37d5d6ed31a7df9\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1772904807 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772904807 +0900\n\nfeat(kirin)!: v0.9.0 — Stream EOS safety, file splits, .mli expansion (#21)\n\n* feat(kirin)!: v0.9.0 — Stream EOS type safety, file splits, .mli expansion\n\nBreaking: `Response.body` Stream/Producer variants now use\n`string option Eio.Stream.t` — `None` signals end-of-stream instead of\nempty string sentinel. Prevents false EOS on protocols where empty\nstring is valid data. Public `yielder`/`producer` types unchanged.\n\nBatch 1 (GLM review carryover):\n- Stream EOS: `string` → `string option` across response, server,\n  stream, sse (7 files). New tests: None-terminates, empty-string-\n  passes-through.\n- Traceparent: `parse_traceparent` now validates lowercase hex chars\n  per W3C Trace Context spec. Tests: uppercase reject, non-hex reject.\n- Random seeding: `Random.self_init ()` at module init for trace ID\n  uniqueness.\n\nBatch 2 (file splits via `include` pattern, public API unchanged):\n- validation.ml 620→430 lines (+validation_schema.ml, +validation_format.ml)\n- testing.ml 563→60 facade (+5 sub-modules)\n- webrtc_adapter.ml 512→302 (+webrtc_config.ml, +webrtc_signaling.ml)\n- metrics.ml 421→154 facade (+5 sub-modules)\n\nBatch 3 (.mli expansion + CI):\n- 8 new .mli files: trace, backpressure, cache, validation, metrics,\n  websocket, sse, cookie. Total: 15 interface files.\n- CI coverage gate: 50% → 60%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(stream): guarantee EOS delivery via Fun.protect\n\nGLM-5 review finding: if producer raises an exception, None (EOS)\nwas never sent to the stream, causing consumer fiber to hang\nindefinitely. Wrap all 3 producer functions (response, file_response,\nfile_inline) with Fun.protect ~finally to guarantee EOS delivery.\n\nAlso narrow broad exception in webrtc_signaling.ml decode_message\nfrom catch-all to Yojson.Safe.Util.Type_error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update CHANGELOG with GLM-5 review fixes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJprGFnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS5UQAJHK0HaBbCcWXd6m85C87fYP\n7J56cKLqiisgxYes6UQjjEKnXuTtns+6rOSXxZTvQ3YlUjN0hTz0lO+Hc60p6cOI\nIgrS+AvQ28HEObFacNAKndNCH6GYpb+VQ8BhycmlEc6DzrVR6ZG2xWVHePWoy5vr\nCLJQtAdFJkBzK64yTp3gmWNH/wwmkVwN1bWIeF0W/zI8Lr+W4d4bQRIFRGpZHS02\nHYNiaYtf3GQL8esf+WLxOWPuuunb2zJhL4m5Qg13Uhy3QuZg9Ctm9ZzG/IQWCBKi\nJcdgIs5NhaeS2TZjVn9AWfP2wMk196OCj/bp8QPg54uYZcNUxL6uWTMcqPvsMdIm\n49bWebLPrJcefY0WFvQ86RFftuMab89aLNxnHRXbG8C9h0nF4ophAOk4YsMkcrDr\nXmeU3IIdy6QkRQ5AKScC9AimrHgMx7fLUMesr9gMWY1Qh2js2qZ8SMoUOqfPmdT4\niRHHLnqwiJzV81ErO7rqKLCltfhxvD+eFgeEYHcnjBPPi4tsSy6n2m91+QIDeCMu\nn8rhHRsdNxbl81wgXe99OVxAJGaRb+gZsuoLJ7fxt99rX5wgKBEoqTQu2S3VBHdZ\n9nYbhj5CCBLnucg9MfLJkV3SgvvvZaUDK0OrfNGxcZEXqMShvPsVAEIZbePST5ki\nOw3Fr05iNPdnn3c0B+88\n=DbXh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-07T17:33:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.