nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/3a248c19d2d1eafbc1891461be0ced3c9f238dbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-07T12:17:37Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-07T12:17:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(kirin): v0.8.0 quality improvements and architecture evolution (#19)\n\n* feat(kirin): add .mli interface files for 7 core modules\n\nAdd interface files establishing clear API boundaries for:\n- request.mli: HTTP request type and accessor functions\n- response.mli: Response construction and helper functions\n- router.mli: Route matching, dispatch, and HTTP method shortcuts\n- middleware.mli: Handler composition and built-in middlewares (CORS, logger, timing)\n- server.mli: Eio-based HTTP server with multicore support\n- stream.mli: Streaming I/O, file uploads, and chunked encoding\n- pool.mli: Generic connection pool with health checks and idle timeout\n\nType exposure strategy:\n- Request.t, Response.t/body, Router.route/segment: concrete (direct field\n  access from 10+ external modules including server, compress, etag, testing,\n  and framework integrations)\n- Pool.t: abstract (internal state not accessed externally)\n- Pool.pooled: concrete (exposed via use_pooled)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(kirin): add coverage job with bisect_ppx and 50% warning gate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(kirin): narrow 46 broad exception handlers to specific types\n\nReplace all `with _ ->` patterns in lib/ with specific exception types:\n- Parse/Conversion (16): Failure _, Yojson.Json_error _, Not_found\n- Cleanup/Resource (9): Unix.Unix_error _, Sys_error _\n- Error Recovery (4): Eio.Io _, End_of_file\n- Framework SSR (17): Yojson.Json_error _, Failure _, Sys_error _\n\nAll 30 files modified, 0 broad exceptions remaining in lib/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: split openapi.ml, add middleware context, fix streaming buffering\n\nA4: Split openapi.ml (868 lines) into three focused modules:\n- openapi_schema.ml: type definitions and builder functions (439 lines)\n- openapi_ui.ml: Swagger UI and ReDoc HTML templates (51 lines)\n- openapi.ml: include Openapi_schema + JSON encoding + wrappers (391 lines)\nBackward compatible via `include Openapi_schema`.\n\nB1: Add heterogeneous middleware context to Request.t using hmap.\n- New `ctx : Hmap.t` field (default: Hmap.empty)\n- `ctx` and `with_ctx` accessors for type-safe state sharing\n- Replaces header-based string workarounds between middleware\n\nB2: Fix streaming buffering bug in server.ml.\n- Previous: Stream/Producer responses fully buffered via\n  read_stream_with_timeout then respond_string (O(n) memory)\n- Now: Stream_source adapter converts Eio.Stream.t to Eio.Flow.source,\n  enabling true chunked streaming via Cohttp_eio.Server.respond (O(1) memory)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(kirin): add lightweight tracing with W3C Trace Context support\n\n- New Trace module: span-based tracing without OpenTelemetry SDK dependency\n- W3C Trace Context: parse/format traceparent headers (version-trace_id-parent_id-flags)\n- Pluggable exporters: Stderr_exporter and Json_exporter module types\n- Tracing middleware: auto root span per request, propagates traceparent, exports on completion\n- Context integration: spans stored in Request.ctx via Hmap (depends on B1)\n- Re-exported as Kirin.Trace in facade module\n- 20 tests covering span ops, W3C parsing, ID generation, context integration, exporters\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"496c313972cdeecb4d6bfbaf850598b1f384acff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/496c313972cdeecb4d6bfbaf850598b1f384acff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/3a248c19d2d1eafbc1891461be0ced3c9f238dbd","verification":{"payload":"tree 496c313972cdeecb4d6bfbaf850598b1f384acff\nparent 94c4491fee46fb204ff0cfa1f08fd7f22082ca54\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1772885857 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772885857 +0900\n\nfeat(kirin): v0.8.0 quality improvements and architecture evolution (#19)\n\n* feat(kirin): add .mli interface files for 7 core modules\n\nAdd interface files establishing clear API boundaries for:\n- request.mli: HTTP request type and accessor functions\n- response.mli: Response construction and helper functions\n- router.mli: Route matching, dispatch, and HTTP method shortcuts\n- middleware.mli: Handler composition and built-in middlewares (CORS, logger, timing)\n- server.mli: Eio-based HTTP server with multicore support\n- stream.mli: Streaming I/O, file uploads, and chunked encoding\n- pool.mli: Generic connection pool with health checks and idle timeout\n\nType exposure strategy:\n- Request.t, Response.t/body, Router.route/segment: concrete (direct field\n  access from 10+ external modules including server, compress, etag, testing,\n  and framework integrations)\n- Pool.t: abstract (internal state not accessed externally)\n- Pool.pooled: concrete (exposed via use_pooled)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(kirin): add coverage job with bisect_ppx and 50% warning gate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(kirin): narrow 46 broad exception handlers to specific types\n\nReplace all `with _ ->` patterns in lib/ with specific exception types:\n- Parse/Conversion (16): Failure _, Yojson.Json_error _, Not_found\n- Cleanup/Resource (9): Unix.Unix_error _, Sys_error _\n- Error Recovery (4): Eio.Io _, End_of_file\n- Framework SSR (17): Yojson.Json_error _, Failure _, Sys_error _\n\nAll 30 files modified, 0 broad exceptions remaining in lib/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: split openapi.ml, add middleware context, fix streaming buffering\n\nA4: Split openapi.ml (868 lines) into three focused modules:\n- openapi_schema.ml: type definitions and builder functions (439 lines)\n- openapi_ui.ml: Swagger UI and ReDoc HTML templates (51 lines)\n- openapi.ml: include Openapi_schema + JSON encoding + wrappers (391 lines)\nBackward compatible via `include Openapi_schema`.\n\nB1: Add heterogeneous middleware context to Request.t using hmap.\n- New `ctx : Hmap.t` field (default: Hmap.empty)\n- `ctx` and `with_ctx` accessors for type-safe state sharing\n- Replaces header-based string workarounds between middleware\n\nB2: Fix streaming buffering bug in server.ml.\n- Previous: Stream/Producer responses fully buffered via\n  read_stream_with_timeout then respond_string (O(n) memory)\n- Now: Stream_source adapter converts Eio.Stream.t to Eio.Flow.source,\n  enabling true chunked streaming via Cohttp_eio.Server.respond (O(1) memory)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(kirin): add lightweight tracing with W3C Trace Context support\n\n- New Trace module: span-based tracing without OpenTelemetry SDK dependency\n- W3C Trace Context: parse/format traceparent headers (version-trace_id-parent_id-flags)\n- Pluggable exporters: Stderr_exporter and Json_exporter module types\n- Tracing middleware: auto root span per request, propagates traceparent, exports on completion\n- Context integration: spans stored in Request.ctx via Hmap (depends on B1)\n- Re-exported as Kirin.Trace in facade module\n- 20 tests covering span ops, W3C parsing, ID generation, context integration, exporters\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJprBdhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASMYQAIDFjklMR2pnsb6nu3m/zHSh\n6oNvsnp+iX1DTlORJQ+wS9SKtgKIiXyOsU/IE84Q8GuLtQxMGZLEvAMJB/ZA1vLc\nNOIaZdNN7twXhv96ZDXsyM/4zSwUvkBs1vGOoPDPkAXmlj2lXpWpes7lHBI4rpIn\nZhQVHcgbfn3rHvhTlBcN7vcNt4niJAlO+JpKJfGaAwQlYMkhKsaDyg2Fiozyb9MW\nyzZYSnWfC6Ixvtw+gXRTuI9ylI4P4LPeyKkXy1ChxeneU3GBkfQ12JhVpLrw1yeI\niT+3RlQIpNX0jIdVO9LkvFdHDt0Y3vbCcLsupZTiS8NiHulm1FawWsVFBfYQ1H9c\n+LQCmRlUUKJ6j1Pb2hVJpjLOLGDo7ei8B1XjwQDxLxwxBpPHs/B6TuNwNf5rhmUp\n/+y4h1C2rhxu0hSI+vmGY6y5omZwXBm72Xi0N+uYDjBZiCf/kMxh/OeINPWYIDbu\nqqIwLqgA3oPUPSkI5aMYFBDCOuO4A+t128LFDGu15vtkTMRj4qtXkp6otd/BL0yl\nL74L3D64AAJ91jgFaLZmWY/JgDEYKaAyNpDu+JnDlsX4NMHxc8GouDICXNWa17LW\nVaxMD3x5d64NriBKZkK+4FHgWifG5NHUqjvdHUe7TQm3/EEqILdHwAUju5FNSB/B\nrAUrWkVn6AuxYRvbvTfh\n=QdqM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-07T12:17:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/3a248c19d2d1eafbc1891461be0ced3c9f238dbd","node_id":"C_kwDOQ_igeNoAKDNhMjQ4YzE5ZDJkMWVhZmJjMTg5MTQ2MWJlMGNlZDNjOWYyMzhkYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik/kirin/commit/94c4491fee46fb204ff0cfa1f08fd7f22082ca54","sha":"94c4491fee46fb204ff0cfa1f08fd7f22082ca54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/94c4491fee46fb204ff0cfa1f08fd7f22082ca54"}],"sha":"3a248c19d2d1eafbc1891461be0ced3c9f238dbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/3a248c19d2d1eafbc1891461be0ced3c9f238dbd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45959991?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeong-sik","id":45959991,"login":"jeong-sik","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTU5OTkx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/94c4491fee46fb204ff0cfa1f08fd7f22082ca54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-20T11:35:40Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-20T11:35:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mcp): Eio direct-style async support + governance/logging (#18)\n\n* feat(mcp): add Eio direct-style async support and governance/logging modules\n\nThread Eio.Switch and clock through MCP server for structured concurrency.\nTool handlers now use a Sync/Async variant type, allowing tools to perform\nconcurrent I/O without blocking the server loop. Add governance layer with\nthree policy levels and logging module with MCP-compliant log emission.\n\n- server.ml: tool_handler = Sync | Async, handle_request ~sw ~clock\n- transport.ml: HTTP transport queues on Eio.Stream with Promise-based send\n- client.ml: session ID management after initialize for HTTP transport\n- protocol.ml: add prompt_message_to_json\n- governance.ml: Development/Production/Enterprise policy levels\n- logging.ml: 8 log levels, handler-based emission\n- mcp_adapter.ml: thread ~sw ~clock to routes, re-export new modules\n- examples: rewrite for add_tool_sync + Eio_main.run context\n- tests: updated for Eio_main.run with Sync handler wrapper\n\n263 tests pass (66 MCP + 197 Kirin).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mcp): address P1 code review findings with regression tests\n\nP1 #1: Protect governance audit_log Queue.t with Eio.Mutex for fiber\nsafety — record_event uses use_rw, readers use use_ro.\n\nP1 #2: Replace weak session ID generation (Hashtbl.hash of timestamp)\nwith Random.bits()-based hex string for collision resistance.\n\nP1 #3: Catch Yojson.Safe.Util.Type_error in logging/setLevel handler\nto prevent unhandled exceptions on malformed params.\n\nP1 #4: Replace disconnected log_level string with Logging.t instance\nin Server.t, wire logging/setLevel to actual Logging.set_level, and\nexpose Server.logging accessor.\n\n11 new tests: 6 governance (including concurrent fiber access),\n5 logging handler (valid/invalid/type-error/missing params/custom level).\n\n77 tests pass (was 66).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(mcp): address P2 code review findings\n\nP2 #1: Bundle sw + clock into eio_ctx record type to reduce parameter\nthreading across the MCP layer. All callsites in server.ml, mcp_adapter.ml,\ntest_mcp.ml, and examples updated.\n\nP2 #2: Add docstring to transport.ml send_http_request explaining why\nPromise.await has no explicit timeout (Eio Switch cancellation model).\n\nP2 #3: MCP spec compliance audit — all 17 method names, 5 JSON-RPC error\ncodes, session state machine, and 2025-11-25 fields verified correct.\nNo code changes needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"54c93a67094e31690620ca2425b8a720410cbe09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/54c93a67094e31690620ca2425b8a720410cbe09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/94c4491fee46fb204ff0cfa1f08fd7f22082ca54","verification":{"payload":"tree 54c93a67094e31690620ca2425b8a720410cbe09\nparent 4521866150fe32c7893929cae92ca68f3fe12272\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1771587340 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771587340 +0900\n\nfeat(mcp): Eio direct-style async support + governance/logging (#18)\n\n* feat(mcp): add Eio direct-style async support and governance/logging modules\n\nThread Eio.Switch and clock through MCP server for structured concurrency.\nTool handlers now use a Sync/Async variant type, allowing tools to perform\nconcurrent I/O without blocking the server loop. Add governance layer with\nthree policy levels and logging module with MCP-compliant log emission.\n\n- server.ml: tool_handler = Sync | Async, handle_request ~sw ~clock\n- transport.ml: HTTP transport queues on Eio.Stream with Promise-based send\n- client.ml: session ID management after initialize for HTTP transport\n- protocol.ml: add prompt_message_to_json\n- governance.ml: Development/Production/Enterprise policy levels\n- logging.ml: 8 log levels, handler-based emission\n- mcp_adapter.ml: thread ~sw ~clock to routes, re-export new modules\n- examples: rewrite for add_tool_sync + Eio_main.run context\n- tests: updated for Eio_main.run with Sync handler wrapper\n\n263 tests pass (66 MCP + 197 Kirin).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(mcp): address P1 code review findings with regression tests\n\nP1 #1: Protect governance audit_log Queue.t with Eio.Mutex for fiber\nsafety — record_event uses use_rw, readers use use_ro.\n\nP1 #2: Replace weak session ID generation (Hashtbl.hash of timestamp)\nwith Random.bits()-based hex string for collision resistance.\n\nP1 #3: Catch Yojson.Safe.Util.Type_error in logging/setLevel handler\nto prevent unhandled exceptions on malformed params.\n\nP1 #4: Replace disconnected log_level string with Logging.t instance\nin Server.t, wire logging/setLevel to actual Logging.set_level, and\nexpose Server.logging accessor.\n\n11 new tests: 6 governance (including concurrent fiber access),\n5 logging handler (valid/invalid/type-error/missing params/custom level).\n\n77 tests pass (was 66).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(mcp): address P2 code review findings\n\nP2 #1: Bundle sw + clock into eio_ctx record type to reduce parameter\nthreading across the MCP layer. All callsites in server.ml, mcp_adapter.ml,\ntest_mcp.ml, and examples updated.\n\nP2 #2: Add docstring to transport.ml send_http_request explaining why\nPromise.await has no explicit timeout (Eio Switch cancellation model).\n\nP2 #3: MCP spec compliance audit — all 17 method names, 5 JSON-RPC error\ncodes, session state machine, and 2025-11-25 fields verified correct.\nNo code changes needed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpmEcMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArTQQAKRMtOtioBq3TOm5ftTRGVVv\nS