k/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeong-sik","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/commits/a0adad31be6c1613d4a0d0f32ce467f6140ccf96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-11T03:56:45Z","email":"45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeong-Sik Yun"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-11T03:56:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Eio 5.x multicore migration — OS Mutex → Eio.Mutex (#6)\n\n* feat: migrate OS Mutex/Condition to Eio-native concurrency\n\n- jobs.ml: Complete rewrite from Thread/OS-Mutex to Eio fibers + Eio.Mutex + Eio.Condition\n- metrics.ml: 5 Mutex.t → Eio.Mutex.t, Unix.gettimeofday → Time_compat.now\n- auth/session.ml: Closure-scoped Mutex → Eio.Mutex\n- webrtc_adapter.ml: 4 Mutex.t + ~19 bare lock/unlock → Eio.Mutex.use_rw/use_ro\n- pool.ml: Mutex + Condition + polling (Unix.sleepf) → Eio.Mutex + Eio.Condition.await\n- backpressure.ml: 4 submodules (Buffer/Channel/RateLimiter/Window) fully migrated\n- shutdown.ml: Polling-based drain → Eio.Condition.await\n- kirin.ml: Updated Jobs module docstring for Eio API\n- examples/high_performance: Restructured for explicit Eio context (clock, sw)\n- tests: Added with_eio helper, all tests pass\n\nKey patterns applied:\n- Eio.Mutex.use_rw ~protect:true for writes, use_ro for reads\n- Eio.Condition.await (positional args) replaces polling loops\n- Time_compat bridge for Unix.gettimeofday/sleepf\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: bump version to 0.6.0 for Eio migration\n\nMinor version bump — OS Mutex/Thread replaced with Eio.Mutex/fibers\nacross 8 modules (jobs, metrics, session, webrtc_adapter, pool,\nbackpressure, shutdown, high_performance example).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wrap Session tests with Eio runtime\n\nSession.create uses Eio.Mutex internally, which requires Eio runtime\ncontext (Effect handler). Added with_eio wrapper and eio_main dep\nto test_auth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wrap Metrics/Shutdown/WebRTC tests with Eio runtime\n\nModules using Eio.Mutex internally (Metrics, Shutdown, WebRTC) need\nan Eio effect handler. Re-shadow with_eio before Metrics section\nsince the Jobs section redefines it with ~sw ~clock labeled args.\n\nRewrite test_shutdown_reject_during_shutdown to use Eio.Fiber.fork\ninstead of Thread.create — OS threads lack Eio effect handler.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wrap Pool/Backpressure tests with Eio runtime\n\nPool and Backpressure modules use Eio.Mutex internally after the\nmigration to Eio-native concurrency. Their tests need to run\ninside Eio_main.run to provide the effect handler.\n\nAll 197 tests now pass: 0 failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"29c12ce099c511f495f3cb3c0737cab0e0d1ec31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/trees/29c12ce099c511f495f3cb3c0737cab0e0d1ec31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeong-sik/kirin/git/commits/a0adad31be6c1613d4a0d0f32ce467f6140ccf96","verification":{"payload":"tree 29c12ce099c511f495f3cb3c0737cab0e0d1ec31\nparent 2d3b550653cc8064b5d60105907a43838c3b71f8\nauthor Jeong-Sik Yun <45959991+jeong-sik@users.noreply.github.com> 1770782205 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770782205 +0900\n\nfeat: Eio 5.x multicore migration — OS Mutex → Eio.Mutex (#6)\n\n* feat: migrate OS Mutex/Condition to Eio-native concurrency\n\n- jobs.ml: Complete rewrite from Thread/OS-Mutex to Eio fibers + Eio.Mutex + Eio.Condition\n- metrics.ml: 5 Mutex.t → Eio.Mutex.t, Unix.gettimeofday → Time_compat.now\n- auth/session.ml: Closure-scoped Mutex → Eio.Mutex\n- webrtc_adapter.ml: 4 Mutex.t + ~19 bare lock/unlock → Eio.Mutex.use_rw/use_ro\n- pool.ml: Mutex + Condition + polling (Unix.sleepf) → Eio.Mutex + Eio.Condition.await\n- backpressure.ml: 4 submodules (Buffer/Channel/RateLimiter/Window) fully migrated\n- shutdown.ml: Polling-based drain → Eio.Condition.await\n- kirin.ml: Updated Jobs module docstring for Eio API\n- examples/high_performance: Restructured for explicit Eio context (clock, sw)\n- tests: Added with_eio helper, all tests pass\n\nKey patterns applied:\n- Eio.Mutex.use_rw ~protect:true for writes, use_ro for reads\n- Eio.Condition.await (positional args) replaces polling loops\n- Time_compat bridge for Unix.gettimeofday/sleepf\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: bump version to 0.6.0 for Eio migration\n\nMinor version bump — OS Mutex/Thread replaced with Eio.Mutex/fibers\nacross 8 modules (jobs, metrics, session, webrtc_adapter, pool,\nbackpressure, shutdown, high_performance example).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wrap Session tests with Eio runtime\n\nSession.create uses Eio.Mutex internally, which requires Eio runtime\ncontext (Effect handler). Added with_eio wrapper and eio_main dep\nto test_auth.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wrap Metrics/Shutdown/WebRTC tests with Eio runtime\n\nModules using Eio.Mutex internally (Metrics, Shutdown, WebRTC) need\nan Eio effect handler. Re-shadow with_eio before Metrics section\nsince the Jobs section redefines it with ~sw ~clock labeled args.\n\nRewrite test_shutdown_reject_during_shutdown to use Eio.Fiber.fork\ninstead of Thread.create — OS threads lack Eio effect handler.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wrap Pool/Backpressure tests with Eio runtime\n\nPool and Backpressure modules use Eio.Mutex internally after the\nmigration to Eio-native concurrency. Their tests need to run\ninside Eio_main.run to provide the effect handler.\n\nAll 197 tests now pass: 0 failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---