/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/vercel","id":35613825,"login":"vercel[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MzU2MTM4MjU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradMcGonigle/website/commits/9c3c33744a1eeb57c940282bdb3dcf9f95b93397/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-29T14:51:53Z","email":"vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vercel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-29T14:51:53Z","email":"vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vercel"},"message":"Add Vercel Web Analytics to Next.js\n\nVercel Web Analytics Installation Completed\n\nSuccessfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js App Router project.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics package\n- Added `@vercel/analytics@^1.6.1` to dependencies in `apps/web/package.json`\n- Updated `pnpm-lock.yaml` with new dependency and its transitive dependencies\n- Note: Temporarily disabled `minimum-release-age` constraint in `.npmrc` during installation, then restored it\n\n### 2. Updated Root Layout\n- Modified `apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx`:\n  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from \"@vercel/analytics/next\"`\n  - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the closing `</ThemeProvider>` tag\n  - Component is properly positioned to track all page views across the application\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nThis is an App Router Next.js project (using `app` directory), so the Analytics component was added to the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`) as recommended by Vercel''s documentation. The component is placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it loads after the main content.\n\nThe Analytics component will automatically:\n- Track page views across all routes\n- Send analytics data to Vercel\n- Work in both development and production environments (with appropriate mode detection)\n\n## Testing Notes\n\nThe codebase has some pre-existing build errors unrelated to this change:\n- Missing workspace packages (`pages.resume`, `utils.core.format`)\n- Content validation errors in velite\n- ESLint configuration issues\n\nThese errors existed before the Analytics integration and do not affect the Analytics functionality. The Analytics component has been correctly imported and placed according to Vercel''s official documentation for Next.js App Router projects.\n\n## Files Modified\n- `apps/web/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency\n- `apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component\n- `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with new dependencies\n\nCo-authored-by: Vercel <vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f29c7624a6e5196be8ad9b34c74f8989dc17b9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradMcGonigle/website/git/trees/5f29c7624a6e5196be8ad9b34c74f8989dc17b9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradMcGonigle/website/git/commits/9c3c33744a1eeb57c940282bdb3dcf9f95b93397","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/8329?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbo