tps://github.com/eustatos","id":20074937,"login":"eustatos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDc0OTM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eustatos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eustatos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eustatos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eustatos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eustatos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eustatos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eustatos/nexus-state/commits/160a4a7df2927aeb0c6330d1c6f3fcdf4cf6e8c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-27T10:55:51Z","email":"astashkinav@gmail.com","name":"eustatos"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-27T10:55:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(core): atom = identity + logic (state in Store)\n\nARCHITECTURE: Atom is a label, not state container\n- Atoms register lazily on first store.get/set/subscribe()\n- State lives in Store, not in Atom\n- Global registry stores atom references + metadata only\n\nCHANGES:\n- atom.ts: Remove immediate registration, lazy-only\n- atom-registry.ts: Store references + metadata (not values)\n- StoreImpl.ts: Fast-path registration in createGetter()\n- TimeTravelController.ts: Store-specific tracking with DEV warnings\n\nBENEFITS:\n✅ SSR Isolation: One atom, different states per store\n✅ Time-travel: Snapshots are store-specific\n✅ Memory: States GC''d with store, atoms lightweight\n✅ Multi-store: Shared atoms work correctly\n\nPERFORMANCE:\n- Baseline (atom creation): 25x faster (124ms → 5ms)\n- Factory (createReactiveValue): 4x faster (285ms → 67ms)\n- Overhead % appears higher due to smaller baseline\n\nTESTS:\n- Updated tests for explicit atom access before capture\n- 1259/1259 core tests passed\n- 99/99 time-travel tests passed\n\nRefs: #71","tree":{"sha":"00a955cd0bd923ec1ef11010cf4ad0997550b1b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eustatos/nexus-state/git/trees/00a955cd0bd923ec1ef11010cf4ad0997550b1b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eustatos/nexus-state/git/commits/160a4a7df2927aeb0c6330d1c6f3fcdf4cf6e8c4","verification":{"payload":"tree 00a955cd0bd923ec1ef11010cf4ad0997550b1b1\nparent e3f4fe9764865ee29f4a999ce7031518b1f47b78\nauthor eustatos <astashkinav@gmail.com> 1774608951 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774608951 +0400\n\nrefactor(core): atom = identity + logic (state in Store)\n\nARCHITECTURE: Atom is a label, not state container\n- Atoms register lazily on first store.get/set/subscribe()\n- State lives in Store, not in Atom\n- Global registry stores atom references + metadata only\n\nCHANGES:\n- atom.ts: Remove immediate registration, lazy-only\n- atom-registry.ts: Store references + metadata (not values)\n- StoreImpl.ts: Fast-path registration in createGetter()\n- TimeTravelController.ts: Store-specific tracking with DEV warnings\n\nBENEFITS:\n✅ SSR Isolation: One atom, different states per store\n✅ Time-travel: Snapshots are store-specific\n✅ Memory: States GC''d with store, atoms lightweight\n✅ Multi-store: Shared atoms work correctly\n\nPERFORMANCE:\n- Baseline (atom creation): 25x faster (124ms → 5ms)\n- Factory (createReactiveValue): 4x faster (285ms → 67ms)\n- Overhead % appears higher due to smaller baseline\n\nTESTS:\n- Updated tests for explicit atom access before capture\n- 1259/1259 core tests passed\n- 99/99 time-travel tests passed\n\nRefs: #71","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpxmI3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxToQAJ6NoQi6uSPtxHrCoSfNI0rF\nZjn3X14luVA04QO/ruTl431U3kUc+SSpnByO+D/t5DH/76AJidVLl62UOTxcEyKL\nmu9yuRG4Kbc6nxv6nRlBf6D1sM1g5IuKdJI2CoGaw/T0bKM9ePKZ4u7Qn5Ew4oFu\nrIqaUH0TrLIGy/Eb1dg28sX8SWvTT4yTs36rTUzxfp4/58j3XzniJpDkwFjpHE2x\nFRgpKgkYJi3L/NmzqCPZcoSrVZhzTNAIZiJBvdDpC/jqRFLD1euOszsMgl11UqDK\nkCIHmtUjE9ds9gNg4jwIexMywmC1fzPU8y2dnOZn1ulHKfWYlCX8lMDF2qIUEJrb\nSDRrOhQ2z