ers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js","id":74466125,"login":"KBH-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDY2MTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/8bc95f7eec901750c185da7a46695f44b40832e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T14:45:26Z","email":"fermionmx@gmail.com","name":"KBH-js"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T14:45:26Z","email":"fermionmx@gmail.com","name":"KBH-js"},"message":"feat(design-system): rem type-scale tokens with no-raw-px lint guardrail\n\n- Add 3xs (0.625rem) / 2xs (0.6875rem) steps to the shared fontSize scale,\n  synced across all four remote theme copies; drop unused 3xl\n- Host tailwind.config now consumes fontSize from @proto/shared/theme, so\n  the shell and remotes share one rem-based type source\n- Replace every arbitrary px class: text-[9|10|11px] -> text-3xs/2xs (21\n  sites), truncate widths snapped to the spacing scale (max-w-56/72/32),\n  exact-size spacers and standalone heights converted to rem arbitraries\n- New local/no-raw-px eslint rule blocks [Npx] arbitrary values in ts/tsx,\n  registered beside no-raw-colors; runtime pixel math stays out of scope\n- Design Tokens app gains a live \"Type scale\" section (name / rem / px /\n  sample per step, derived from the token source) and updated ko/en\n  guardrail copy\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3c6b263692db406bbb8f8457cfa6df8805e6e577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/trees/3c6b263692db406bbb8f8457cfa6df8805e6e577"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/commits/8bc95f7eec901750c185da7a46695f44b40832e2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74466125?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js","id":74466125,"login":"KBH-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDY2MTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js/proto/commit/8bc95f7eec901750c185da7a46695f44b40832e2","node_id":"C_kwDORAQN1NoAKDhiYzk1ZjdlZWM5MDE3NTBjMTg1ZGE3YTQ2Njk1ZjQ0YjQwODMyZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js/proto/commit/0e2aea8499948d69b3ffca363c9a052564e443d6","sha":"0e2aea8499948d69b3ffca363c9a052564e443d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/0e2aea8499948d69b3ffca363c9a052564e443d6"}],"sha":"8bc95f7eec901750c185da7a46695f44b40832e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/8bc95f7eec901750c185da7a46695f44b40832e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74466125?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js","id":74466125,"login":"KBH-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDY2MTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/0e2aea8499948d69b3ffca363c9a052564e443d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T14:45:06Z","email":"fermionmx@gmail.com","name":"KBH-js"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T14:45:06Z","email":"fermionmx@gmail.com","name":"KBH-js"},"message":"fix(tour): readable type scale and mobile sheet layout for first-run tour\n\n- Bump all tour card text up a step (progress 10->12px, title 14->16/18px,\n  body 12->14px, buttons 12->14px with taller tap targets)\n- Below the sm breakpoint the card becomes an edge-to-edge sheet docked to\n  the top or bottom (whichever half the spotlighted anchor is not in),\n  with full-width buttons; tracked live via matchMedia so rotation reflows\n- Desktop keeps the anchored-beside-the-element placement (300->340px card)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2689c0f70046991fc62954a4dff8606b04a49c49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/trees/2689c0f70046991fc62954a4dff8606b04a49c49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/commits/0e2aea8499948d69b3ffca363c9a052564e443d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74466125?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js","id":74466125,"login":"KBH-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDY2MTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js/proto/commit/0e2aea8499948d69b3ffca363c9a052564e443d6","node_id":"C_kwDORAQN1NoAKDBlMmFlYTg0OTk5NDhkNjliM2ZmY2EzNjNjOWEwNTI1NjRlNDQzZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js/proto/commit/fa40c9fb8de070afad73caa514b84607c90133e8","sha":"fa40c9fb8de070afad73caa514b84607c90133e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/fa40c9fb8de070afad73caa514b84607c90133e8"}],"sha":"0e2aea8499948d69b3ffca363c9a052564e443d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/0e2aea8499948d69b3ffca363c9a052564e443d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74466125?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js","id":74466125,"login":"KBH-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDY2MTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/fa40c9fb8de070afad73caa514b84607c90133e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T13:55:56Z","email":"74466125+KBH-js@users.noreply.github.com","name":"KBH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T13:55:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(registry): survive dev-HMR store re-instantiation in app registry init (#17)\n\ninitializeAppRegistry() cached its promise in a module-level flag forever,\nso when HMR re-seeded the zustand registry store (locals only, status\n''loading'') the remote catalog was never re-merged and the desktop lost its\nremote icons until a manual reload.\n\n- Guard only the in-flight fetch (StrictMode double-invoke joins it) and\n  judge \"already initialized\" from store state: no-op once status left\n  ''loading'' (ready/degraded — no retry loop), re-run after a store reset.\n- Dev-only self-heal: a freshly HMR-instantiated module kicks the\n  state-guarded init itself, since Fast Refresh re-renders App without\n  re-firing its [] mount effect. import.meta.webpackHot is undefined in\n  prod builds and Vitest, so production boots exactly once as before.\n- Add src/registry/appRegistry.test.ts covering merge/ready, no-op when\n  ready, concurrent join, re-run after store reset, degraded fallback.\n\nVerified live: editing appRegistry.ts previously dropped all remote icons\n(remote 0개); with the fix the next HMR update self-heals and further HMR\ncycles keep all 4 remotes without reload.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ed309bd41a6e24b2c98e403d53106b0ea32a68d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/trees/ed309bd41a6e24b2c98e403d53106b0ea32a68d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/commits/fa40c9fb8de070afad73caa514b84607c90133e8","verification":{"payload":"tree ed309bd41a6e24b2c98e403d53106b0ea32a68d7\nparent 0f9d3efdc4b128d5340920f73ba41397ecc30c07\nauthor KBH <74466125+KBH-js@users.noreply.github.com> 1784123756 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784123756 +0900\n\nfix(registry): survive dev-HMR store re-instantiation in app registry init (#17)\n\ninitializeAppRegistry() cached its promise in a module-level flag forever,\nso when HMR re-seeded the zustand registry store (locals only, status\n''loading'') the remote catalog was never re-merged and the desktop lost its\nremote icons until a manual reload.\n\n- Guard only the in-flight fetch (StrictMode double-invoke joins it) and\n  judge \"already initialized\" from store state: no-op once status left\n  ''loading'' (ready/degraded — no retry loop), re-run after a store reset.\n- Dev-only self-heal: a freshly HMR-instantiated module kicks the\n  state-guarded init itself, since Fast Refresh re-renders App without\n  re-firing its [] mount effect. import.meta.webpackHot is undefined in\n  prod builds and Vitest, so production boots exactly once as before.\n- Add src/registry/appRegistry.test.ts covering merge/ready, no-op when\n  ready, concurrent join, re-run after store reset, degraded fallback.\n\nVerified live: editing appRegistry.ts previously dropped all remote icons\n(remote 0개); with the fix the next HMR update self-heals and further HMR\ncycles keep all 4 remotes without reload.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV5FsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcxQQAC