per, invisible on the light glass rail\n(white-on-white, measured rgba(255,255,255,0.44) rail). Labels now\npair gray-800/gray-100 with the lg-text glass shadow token (white lift\non light, dark drop on dark), and the hover/active/focus feedback --\nalso white-on-white in light -- gets black-alpha light variants\nmatching the taskbar convention.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf829cb328009aa162b61109f822ce4dcb2c4edc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/trees/bf829cb328009aa162b61109f822ce4dcb2c4edc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/commits/468af47f4b9c7264e720eca0fbefa61d48db6d76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74466125?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js","id":74466125,"login":"KBH-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDY2MTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js/proto/commit/468af47f4b9c7264e720eca0fbefa61d48db6d76","node_id":"C_kwDORAQN1NoAKDQ2OGFmNDdmNGI5YzcyNjRlNzIwZWNhMGZiZWZhNjFkNDhkYjZkNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js/proto/commit/c7744b5773e1256ceda4690b45dbea5450b3980f","sha":"c7744b5773e1256ceda4690b45dbea5450b3980f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/c7744b5773e1256ceda4690b45dbea5450b3980f"}],"sha":"468af47f4b9c7264e720eca0fbefa61d48db6d76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/468af47f4b9c7264e720eca0fbefa61d48db6d76"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74466125?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js","id":74466125,"login":"KBH-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDY2MTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/41f03da81bff4276f0bf1af31fcbbacfe5c047b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T13:29:43Z","email":"74466125+KBH-js@users.noreply.github.com","name":"KBH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T13:29:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(i18n): rewrite About copy, drop taskbar empty-state label (#15)\n\nReplace the About app''s Korean copy with the finalized text and mirror\nevery change into the en bundle:\n\n- honesty banner now states the clean-room reproduction is spec/architecture\n  driven via AI assisted coding\n- federation and theming claims drop their trailing caveats\n- runtime decision motivates per-user app personalization\n- singleton decision reframed around shared-module perf + version match\n\nDrop the claims (testing, compiler, domain, aidx) and decisions (recovery,\ncss) that are no longer part of the page, along with the code only they\nused: the source/none claim actions, act.source/act.test keys, the REPO\nconstant and four now-unused icon imports.\n\nRemove the taskbar''s \"열린 창 없음\" empty state — the item container just\nrenders nothing when no windows are open.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d7b869af26b7d3fb41c54b08b67e2961b33f15c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/trees/d7b869af26b7d3fb41c54b08b67e2961b33f15c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/commits/41f03da81bff4276f0bf1af31fcbbacfe5c047b5","verification":{"payload":"tree d7b869af26b7d3fb41c54b08b67e2961b33f15c1\nparent f672cba3bd441b1d78b8fcced9f4f9e2cec68a16\nauthor KBH <74466125+KBH-js@users.noreply.github.com> 1784122183 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784122183 +0900\n\nrefactor(i18n): rewrite About copy, drop taskbar empty-state label (#15)\n\nReplace the About app''s Korean copy with the finalized text and mirror\nevery change into the en bundle:\n\n- honesty banner now states the clean-room reproduction is spec/architecture\n  driven via AI assisted coding\n- federation and theming claims drop their trailing caveats\n- runtime decision motivates per-user app personalization\n- singleton decision reframed around shared-module perf + version match\n\nDrop the claims (testing, compiler, domain, aidx) and decisions (recovery,\ncss) that are no longer part of the page, along with the code only they\nused: the source/none claim actions, act.source/act.test keys, the REPO\nconstant and four now-unused icon imports.\n\nRemove the taskbar''s \"열린 창 없음\" empty state — the item container just\nrenders nothing when no windows are open.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAAB