vatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74466125?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/KBH-js","id":74466125,"login":"KBH-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NDY2MTI1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KBH-js","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/commits/3355aa916cbaa926553fb0d794f7239fdf26c6f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T14:40:57Z","email":"74466125+KBH-js@users.noreply.github.com","name":"KBH"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T14:40:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Liquid Glass (macOS Tahoe) theme — shared <LiquidGlass> singleton, glass shell chrome & honest boot splash (#12)\n\n* feat: Liquid Glass (Tahoe) material — shared <LiquidGlass> singleton + tokens\n\nAdd the reusable Liquid Glass surface to the shared layer, registered as a\nModule Federation singleton like React (host provides one instance; remotes can\nconsume it, standalone-fallbacking to their own copy).\n\n- packages/shared/LiquidGlass.tsx: variant/blur/saturate/tint/chromaticAberration\n  /radius/inline props; auto-installs the shared filters on mount.\n- packages/shared/glassFilters.ts: one global SVG <defs> (turbulence displacement\n  + RGB-split chroma), injected once.\n- packages/shared/glass.css: refracting material — single backdrop-filter driven\n  by --lg-backdrop / --lg-refract-fn toggles (the pipeline drops filter-only\n  rules, and --lg-blur is set inline), @supports fallback to plain glassmorphism,\n  prefers-reduced-transparency/-motion handling, .lg-dragging perf downgrade.\n- host rsbuild: shared ''@proto/shared/glass'' singleton + source.include for the\n  workspace TSX; tailwind glass tokens; index.css --glass-* theme tokens (light\n  :root / dark .dark) + Aqua traffic-light styles.\n- theme.js: colourful light/dark wallpapers so glass has hues to refract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: apply Liquid Glass to dock, sidebar, window chrome, menu & About\n\n- Bottom dock: floating centred Liquid Glass shelf (variant=\"dock\").\n- New left sidebar Dock: vertical glass rail of app launchers.\n- Window frame: variant=\"window\" panel; titlebar goes translucent so the glass\n  shows through; content area transparent.\n- Start menu dropdown: variant=\"menu\".\n- About window: translucent panel; claim/decision/deploy cards → variant=\"card\";\n  action pills + tag badges (\"live\"/\"인스펙터에서 보기\"/\"가이드 투어 다시 보기\")\n  → variant=\"button\" (semantic colour kept on text/icon).\n- Glossy Aqua traffic lights (close/min/max) with crisp centred SVG glyphs,\n  replacing the mis-rendered pseudo-element glyphs.\n- Perf: WindowFrame toggles the root .lg-dragging class during drag.\n- TASKBAR_HEIGHT 52→64 to seat the detached floating dock + gap.\n\nAll raw colours stay in CSS/tokens to satisfy the no-raw-colors guardrail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: themed minimal boot splash + glass loading fallback\n\n- BootScreen: drop the scripted stepper + fake progress bar; keep a minimal\n  Liquid Glass card (logo + accent spinner) over the colour wallpaper. Gate\n  honestly on the real registry status (holds until initializeAppRegistry\n  resolves to ready/degraded) with only a small min-duration floor to avoid a\n  flash — no artificial 1200ms. Boot gate ownership moves App → BootScreen.\n- LoadingFallback: transparent so the window glass shows through while a remote\n  loads; accent spinner + lifted label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"07774abe2ddc30f81bfb22dac49d8f789c920159","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/trees/07774abe2ddc30f81bfb22dac49d8f789c920159"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/KBH-js/proto/git/commits/3355aa916cbaa926553fb0d794f7239fdf26c6f7","verification":{"payload":"tree 07774abe2ddc30f81bfb22dac49d8f789c920159\nparent f86e470d9875522f280fd970393d736b9d36a046\nauthor KBH <74466125+KBH-js@users.noreply.github.com> 1783953657 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783953657 +0900\n\nfeat: Liquid Glass (macOS Tahoe) theme — shared <LiquidGlass> singleton, glass shell chrome & honest boot splash (#12)\n\n* feat: Liquid Glass (Tahoe) material — shared <LiquidGlass> singleton + tokens\n\nAdd the reusable Liquid Glass surface to the shared layer, registered as a\nModule Federation singleton like React (host provides one instance; remotes can\nconsume it, standalone-fallbacking to their own copy).\n\n- packages/shared/LiquidGlass.tsx: variant/blur/saturate/tint/chromaticAberration\n  /radius/inline props; auto-installs the shared filters on mount.\n- packages/shared/glassFilters.ts: one global SVG <defs> (turbulence displacement\n  + RGB-split chroma), injected once.\n- packages/shared/glass.css: refracting material — single backdrop-filter driven\n  by --lg-backdrop / --lg-refract-fn toggles (the pipeline drops filter-only\n  rules, and --lg-blur is set inline), @supports fallback to plain glassmorphism,\n  prefers-reduced-transparency/-motion handling, .lg-dragging perf downgrade.\n- host rsbuild: shared ''@proto/shared/glass'' singleton + source.include for the\n  workspace TSX; tailwind glass tokens; index.css --glass-* theme tokens (light\n  :root / dark .dark) + Aqua traffic-light styles.\n- theme.js: colourful light/dark wallpapers so glass has hues to refract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: apply Liquid Glass to dock, sidebar, window chrome, menu & About\n\n- Bottom dock: floating centred Liquid Glass shelf (variant=\"dock\").\n- New left sidebar Dock: vertical glass rail of app launchers.\n- Window frame: variant=\"window\" panel; titlebar goes translucent so the glass\n  shows through; content area transparent.\n- Start menu dropdown: variant=\"menu\".\n- About window: translucent panel; claim/decision/deploy cards → variant=\"card\";\n  action pills + tag badges (\"live\"/\"인스펙터에서 보기\"/\"가이드 투어 다시 보기\")\n  → variant=\"button\" (semantic colour kept on text/icon).\n- Glossy Aqua traffic lights (close/min/max) with crisp centred SVG glyphs,\n  replacing the mis-rendered pseudo-element glyphs.\n- Perf: WindowFrame toggles the root .lg-dragging class during drag.\n- TASKBAR_HEIGHT 52→64 to seat the detached floating dock + gap.\n\nAll raw colours stay in CSS/tokens to satisfy the no-raw-colors guardrail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: themed minimal boot splash + glass loading fallback\n\n- BootScreen: drop the scripted stepper + fake progress bar; keep a minimal\n  Liquid Glass card (logo + accent spinner) over the colour wallpaper. Gate\n  honestly on the real registry status (holds until initializeAppRegistry\n  resolves to ready/degraded) with only a small min-duration floor to avoid a\n  flash — no artificial 1200ms. Boot gate ownership moves App → BootScreen.\n- LoadingFallback: transparent so the window glass shows through while a remote\n  loads; accent spinner + lifted label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVPj5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA284QAD1JcKrZ