d_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/kweaver-ai/dip-for-supply-chain/commit/8f0aeeefaf870fe18f41d9aee5f9ba281db5baed","node_id":"C_kwDORAWc09oAKDhmMGFlZWVmYWY4NzBmZTE4ZjQxZDlhZWU1ZjliYTI4MWRiNWJhZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kweaver-ai/dip-for-supply-chain/commit/38218dea6b33ff06d658c9456eb9f57723a6b7aa","sha":"38218dea6b33ff06d658c9456eb9f57723a6b7aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kweaver-ai/dip-for-supply-chain/commits/38218dea6b33ff06d658c9456eb9f57723a6b7aa"}],"sha":"8f0aeeefaf870fe18f41d9aee5f9ba281db5baed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kweaver-ai/dip-for-supply-chain/commits/8f0aeeefaf870fe18f41d9aee5f9ba281db5baed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19240301?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leecky","id":19240301,"login":"leecky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjQwMzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kweaver-ai/dip-for-supply-chain/commits/38218dea6b33ff06d658c9456eb9f57723a6b7aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-16T16:03:06Z","email":"10833833@qq.com","name":"leecky"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-16T16:03:06Z","email":"10833833@qq.com","name":"leecky"},"message":"Complete the development of the complete production mode for the product:\nDefinition: The product complete set production mode refers to the fact that the production plans for each level of products and components adopt an inverted arrangement mode. The production plans are calculated based on inverted logic to ensure that all sub-level materials are complete before starting the production of the upper level. The principles are as follows:\nThe quantitative relationship of BOM expansion for products and components/materials is as follows: The required quantity of sub-components/materials = (planned production quantity of upper-level products/components * usage of sub-components)/(1- loss rate). Note: The child_quantity and loss_rate are derived from the product BOM object. The default loss_rate is a percentage. If it is greater than 1, divide it by 100.\n-2. If the current inventory quantity of a component or material is greater than the required quantity, it indicates that the component or material is ready. The progress bar can be expressed as one day. Otherwise, it indicates that the material is not ready and needs to be purchased externally or the components need to be produced. Objects that are ready are indicated by green progress, and those that are not ready are indicated by yellow.\n-3. The temporal distribution relationship of products, components, and material objects on the Gantt chart is as follows:\nFirst, clarify the product. Define the end time of the product to the end time of the production plan. From here, work backward to determine that the assembly start time of the product = end time - product assembly duration.\nThen, work backward layer by layer. The end time of all objects at each level = the start time of the previous level -1.\nIf the start time of the final material object (actual_start_time) is earlier than the start time of the production plan (start_time of the factory plan object), it means that it cannot end at the agreed end time. Then, adjust the start and end times of all objects backward. Adjust the number of days = start_time - actual_start_time.\nIf the start time of the final material object (actual_start_time) is later than the start time of the production plan (start_time of the factory plan object), it means that the production plan time can be completed ahead of schedule. Then, adjust the start and end times of all objects forward. Adjust the number of days = actual_start_time - start_time.","tree":{"sha":"f83bc5e01b6cfb06bf775bcb2d60ba0bad1ab2c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kweaver-ai/dip-for-supply-chain/git/trees/f83bc5e01b6cfb06bf775bcb2d60ba0bad1ab2c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kweaver-ai/dip-for-supply-chain/git/commits/38218dea6b33ff06d658c9456eb9f57723a6b7aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19240301?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leecky","id":19240301,"login":"leecky","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjQwMzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leecky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.c